window.IELTS_TOPIC={"topic":12,"en":"Earth Science & Space","zh":"地球科學與太空","items":[{"w":"crust","pos":"n.","def":"the hard outer layer of the Earth","cn":"地殼","s":"The Earth's ________ is very thin compared with the rest of the planet, but it is the only layer that people can actually walk on.","zh":"和地球的其他部分相比，地球的地殼非常薄，但它是人們唯一能夠真正行走的一層。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A1","t":"地殼"},{"w":"mantle","pos":"n.","def":"the thick hot layer between the crust and the core","cn":"地函","s":"Our geography teacher explained that rock in the ________ moves very slowly, and this movement pushes the plates above it.","zh":"我們的地理老師解釋說，地函中的岩石移動得非常緩慢，而這種移動推動了上方的板塊。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A2","t":"地函"},{"w":"outer core","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the liquid metal layer around the Earth's centre","cn":"外核","s":"Scientists believe that the ______ ______ is made of liquid iron, and its movement creates the Earth's magnetic field.","zh":"科學家相信外核是由液態鐵構成的，而它的流動產生了地球的磁場。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A3","t":"外核"},{"w":"inner core","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the solid metal ball at the very centre of the Earth","cn":"內核","s":"The ______ ______ is hotter than the surface of the sun, but it stays solid because the pressure there is extremely high.","zh":"內核比太陽表面還要熱，但因為那裡的壓力極高，所以它保持固態。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A4","t":"內核"},{"w":"lithosphere","pos":"n.","def":"the rigid outer shell made of crust and upper mantle","cn":"岩石圈","s":"The ________ is broken into large pieces, so the land we live on is always moving a few centimetres every year.","zh":"岩石圈破裂成許多大塊，所以我們居住的陸地每年都在移動幾公分。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A5","t":"岩石圈"},{"w":"asthenosphere","pos":"n.","def":"the soft, partly melted layer under the lithosphere","cn":"軟流圈","s":"The plates slide over the ________ because this layer is soft enough to flow, although it is still mostly solid rock.","zh":"板塊在軟流圈上滑動，因為這一層軟到可以流動，雖然它大部分仍是固態岩石。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A6","t":"軟流圈"},{"w":"tectonic plate","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a huge moving piece of the Earth's outer shell","cn":"構造板塊","s":"Taiwan sits where two ______ ______ meet, so the island has many earthquakes and its mountains are still rising.","zh":"臺灣位於兩個構造板塊交會的地方，所以這座島嶼地震頻繁，而且山脈仍在持續升高。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A7","t":"構造板塊"},{"w":"plate tectonics","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the theory that the Earth's surface is made of moving plates","cn":"板塊構造論","s":"______ ______ explains why earthquakes happen in certain places, and it also helps us understand how mountains are formed.","zh":"板塊構造論解釋了為什麼地震會發生在某些地方，而且它也幫助我們了解山脈是如何形成的。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A8","t":"板塊構造論"},{"w":"continental drift","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the slow movement of continents across the Earth","cn":"大陸漂移","s":"Alfred Wegener first suggested the idea of ______ ______, but many scientists laughed at him because he could not explain how it worked.","zh":"韋格納首先提出大陸漂移的概念，但許多科學家嘲笑他，因為他無法解釋其運作方式。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A9","t":"大陸漂移"},{"w":"supercontinent","pos":"n.","def":"one huge landmass made of many joined continents","cn":"超大陸","s":"Millions of years ago, all the land formed one ________, and dinosaurs could walk from today's Africa to South America.","zh":"數百萬年前，所有陸地形成一個超大陸，而恐龍可以從今天的非洲走到南美洲。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A10","t":"超大陸"},{"w":"Pangaea","pos":"n.","def":"the supercontinent that existed about 300 million years ago","cn":"盤古大陸","s":"The coastlines of Africa and South America fit together like puzzle pieces, so scientists think they were once joined in ________.","zh":"非洲和南美洲的海岸線像拼圖一樣能拼在一起，所以科學家認為它們曾經在盤古大陸中相連。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A11","t":"盤古大陸"},{"w":"fault line","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a long crack in the Earth's crust where rocks move","cn":"斷層線","s":"The new school was built far away from the ______ ______, because the city wanted to keep students safe during earthquakes.","zh":"新學校蓋在離斷層線很遠的地方，因為市政府希望在地震時保護學生的安全。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A12","t":"斷層線"},{"w":"subduction","pos":"n.","def":"when one plate slides under another plate","cn":"隱沒作用","s":"________ happens when a heavy ocean plate sinks under a lighter plate, and this process often creates deep trenches and volcanoes.","zh":"當沉重的海洋板塊沉入較輕的板塊之下時，就會發生隱沒作用，而這個過程常常形成深海溝和火山。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A13","t":"隱沒作用"},{"w":"convection current","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a circular flow of heat in a liquid or soft solid","cn":"對流","s":"Hot rock rises and cool rock sinks in the mantle, so these ______ ______ slowly drag the plates across the planet.","zh":"地函中熱的岩石上升、冷的岩石下沉，所以這些對流緩慢地拖動板塊在地球上移動。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A14","t":"對流"},{"w":"magnetic field","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the invisible area of magnetic force around the Earth","cn":"磁場","s":"The Earth's ______ ______ protects us from harmful particles from the sun, and it also makes a compass needle point north.","zh":"地球的磁場保護我們免於來自太陽的有害粒子，而且它也讓指南針的指針指向北方。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A15","t":"磁場"},{"w":"oceanic crust","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the thin, heavy crust under the oceans","cn":"海洋地殼","s":"______ ______ is younger and heavier than the land beneath our cities, so it usually sinks when two plates collide.","zh":"海洋地殼比我們城市底下的陸地更年輕也更重，所以當兩個板塊相撞時它通常會下沉。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A16","t":"海洋地殼"},{"w":"continental crust","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the thick, lighter crust that forms the land","cn":"大陸地殼","s":"______ ______ can be more than 50 kilometres thick under high mountains, while it is much thinner under flat plains.","zh":"在高山底下，大陸地殼可以超過五十公里厚，而在平坦的平原底下則薄得多。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A17","t":"大陸地殼"},{"w":"plate boundary","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the edge where two tectonic plates meet","cn":"板塊邊界","s":"Japan lies on an active ______ ______, so children there practise earthquake safety at school several times a year.","zh":"日本位於活躍的板塊邊界上，所以那裡的孩子每年在學校練習好幾次地震安全演練。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A18","t":"板塊邊界"},{"w":"mid-ocean ridge","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a long underwater mountain chain where new crust forms","cn":"中洋脊","s":"The ________ ________ runs through the middle of the Atlantic Ocean, and new rock is created there as the plates move apart.","zh":"中洋脊貫穿大西洋中央，而當板塊彼此分離時，新的岩石就在那裡生成。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A19","t":"中洋脊"},{"w":"rift valley","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a long valley formed when the land splits apart","cn":"裂谷","s":"East Africa has a huge ______ ______, and some geologists think the continent may eventually split into two parts.","zh":"東非有一條巨大的裂谷，有些地質學家認為這塊大陸最終可能會分裂成兩部分。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A20","t":"裂谷"},{"w":"uplift","pos":"n.","def":"the rising of land caused by forces inside the Earth","cn":"抬升","s":"The Himalayas are still growing because of continuous ________, and the mountains rise a few millimetres higher every year.","zh":"喜馬拉雅山脈仍在增高，因為持續的抬升作用，而山脈每年都會升高幾毫米。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A21","t":"抬升"},{"w":"fold","pos":"n.","def":"a bend in rock layers caused by pressure","cn":"褶皺","s":"You can see a huge ________ in the rock beside the highway, and it shows how strong the pressure inside the Earth can be.","zh":"你可以在公路旁的岩石上看到一個巨大的褶皺，而它顯示出地球內部的壓力有多強。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A22","t":"褶皺"},{"w":"geology","pos":"n.","def":"the study of rocks and the Earth's history","cn":"地質學","s":"My cousin chose to study ________ at university because she loves hiking, and she wants to understand how mountains were made.","zh":"我表姊在大學選擇念地質學，因為她熱愛健行，而且她想了解山是怎麼形成的。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A23","t":"地質學"},{"w":"geophysicist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies the physical processes of the Earth","cn":"地球物理學家","s":"The ________ used special sensors to study the ground under the city, and her report helped engineers design safer buildings.","zh":"那位地球物理學家使用特殊感測器研究城市底下的地層，而她的報告幫助工程師設計出更安全的建築。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A24","t":"地球物理學家"},{"w":"seafloor spreading","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the process where new ocean floor forms and moves apart","cn":"海底擴張","s":"______ ______ slowly makes the Atlantic Ocean wider, so the distance between Europe and America grows every year.","zh":"海底擴張慢慢讓大西洋變得更寬，所以歐洲和美洲之間的距離每年都在增加。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A25","t":"海底擴張"},{"w":"geological","pos":"adj.","def":"related to rocks and the history of the Earth","cn":"地質的","s":"The park has many interesting ________ features, so geography teachers often bring their students there on field trips.","zh":"這座公園有許多有趣的地質特徵，所以地理老師常常帶學生去那裡校外教學。","part":"A","sec":"Earth's Structure & Plate Tectonics 地球結構與板塊構造","lab":"A26","t":"地質"},{"w":"volcano","pos":"n.","def":"a mountain that can send out hot rock, gas and ash","cn":"火山","s":"Mount Fuji is actually a ________, but it has not erupted for over 300 years, so millions of tourists climb it safely.","zh":"富士山其實是一座火山，但它已經超過三百年沒有噴發，所以數百萬名遊客能安全地攀登。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A27","t":"火山"},{"w":"volcanic","pos":"adj.","def":"produced by or related to a volcano","cn":"火山的","s":"Yangmingshan has rich ________ soil, so farmers grow excellent vegetables there, and visitors enjoy the hot springs too.","zh":"陽明山有肥沃的火山土壤，所以農民在那裡種出優質蔬菜，而且遊客也很喜歡那裡的溫泉。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A28","t":"火山"},{"w":"eruption","pos":"n.","def":"when a volcano suddenly throws out lava, ash and gas","cn":"噴發","s":"The ________ sent ash high into the sky, so hundreds of flights across Europe were cancelled for almost a week.","zh":"那次噴發把火山灰噴到高空中，所以歐洲各地數百個航班被取消將近一週。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A29","t":"噴發"},{"w":"erupt","pos":"v.","def":"to suddenly throw out lava, ash or gas","cn":"（火山）爆發","s":"Scientists cannot say exactly when the volcano will ________ again, but they watch it closely every day to warn local people.","zh":"科學家無法確切說出那座火山何時會再次爆發，但他們每天密切監測，以便警告當地居民。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A30","t":"爆發"},{"w":"magma","pos":"n.","def":"hot liquid rock under the Earth's surface","cn":"岩漿","s":"When ________ rises toward the surface, the ground may swell slightly, and scientists use this sign to predict eruptions.","zh":"當岩漿朝地表上升時，地面可能會稍微隆起，而科學家利用這個跡象來預測噴發。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A31","t":"岩漿"},{"w":"lava","pos":"n.","def":"hot liquid rock that comes out of a volcano","cn":"熔岩","s":"The red ________ flowed slowly down the mountain, but it destroyed several houses because nobody could stop it.","zh":"紅色的熔岩緩緩流下山，但它摧毀了好幾棟房子，因為沒有人能阻擋它。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A32","t":"熔岩"},{"w":"ash cloud","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a huge cloud of tiny rock pieces from a volcano","cn":"火山灰雲","s":"The airline cancelled our flight because a large ______ ______ was moving toward the airport, and the ash could damage engines.","zh":"航空公司取消了我們的班機，因為一大片火山灰雲正往機場移動，而火山灰可能會損壞引擎。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A33","t":"火山灰雲"},{"w":"crater","pos":"n.","def":"a large bowl-shaped hole at the top of a volcano or made by an impact","cn":"火山口；坑洞","s":"We hiked to the edge of the ________ early in the morning, and we could see steam rising from the bottom.","zh":"我們一大早健行到火山口邊緣，而且我們能看到蒸氣從底部冒出來。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A34","t":"火山口"},{"w":"caldera","pos":"n.","def":"a huge hollow formed when a volcano collapses","cn":"破火山口","s":"After the giant eruption, the top of the mountain fell in and formed a ________, which later filled with water and became a lake.","zh":"那次巨大噴發後，山頂崩塌形成了一個破火山口，後來積水變成了一座湖。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A35","t":"破火山口"},{"w":"pyroclastic flow","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a fast, deadly cloud of hot gas and rock","cn":"火山碎屑流","s":"A ______ ______ can move faster than a car, so people living near the volcano must leave as soon as officials warn them.","zh":"火山碎屑流可以移動得比汽車還快，所以住在火山附近的人一接到官員警告就必須離開。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A36","t":"火山碎屑流"},{"w":"hot spring","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a natural pool of water heated underground","cn":"溫泉","s":"After a long day of hiking, we relaxed in a ______ ______, and the warm water made our tired legs feel much better.","zh":"經過一整天的健行後，我們在溫泉裡放鬆，而溫暖的泉水讓我們疲憊的雙腿舒服多了。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A37","t":"溫泉"},{"w":"geyser","pos":"n.","def":"a hot spring that shoots water and steam into the air","cn":"間歇泉","s":"Tourists waited patiently for the ________ to shoot water into the air, and everyone cheered when it finally happened.","zh":"遊客耐心地等待間歇泉把水噴向空中，而當它終於噴發時，每個人都歡呼起來。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A38","t":"間歇泉"},{"w":"earthquake","pos":"n.","def":"a sudden shaking of the ground","cn":"地震","s":"The ________ woke me up at three in the morning, so I hid under my desk until the shaking stopped.","zh":"那場地震在凌晨三點把我搖醒，所以我躲在書桌底下直到搖晃停止。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A39","t":"地震"},{"w":"tremor","pos":"n.","def":"a small shaking of the ground","cn":"輕微震動","s":"We felt a slight ________ during dinner, but nobody panicked because small shakes are common in Taiwan.","zh":"我們在晚餐時感覺到輕微的震動，但沒有人驚慌，因為小地震在臺灣很常見。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A40","t":"震動"},{"w":"aftershock","pos":"n.","def":"a smaller earthquake that follows a big one","cn":"餘震","s":"Many families slept outside that night because they were afraid of another ________, and the shaking continued for days.","zh":"那天晚上許多家庭睡在戶外，因為他們害怕再有餘震，而搖晃持續了好幾天。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A41","t":"餘震"},{"w":"foreshock","pos":"n.","def":"a smaller earthquake that comes before a bigger one","cn":"前震","s":"Nobody realised that the small shake was a ________, so people were shocked when a much stronger quake hit an hour later.","zh":"沒有人意識到那次小搖晃是前震，所以一小時後更強的地震來襲時，大家都嚇壞了。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A42","t":"前震"},{"w":"seismograph","pos":"n.","def":"a machine that measures and records earthquakes","cn":"地震儀","s":"The ________ in the school lab recorded the earthquake clearly, and our science teacher showed us the zigzag lines the next day.","zh":"學校實驗室裡的地震儀清楚地記錄了那場地震，而我們的自然老師隔天給我們看那些鋸齒狀的線條。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A43","t":"地震儀"},{"w":"seismologist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies earthquakes","cn":"地震學家","s":"The ________ explained on TV that the earthquake was not dangerous, but she reminded viewers to prepare emergency kits.","zh":"那位地震學家在電視上解釋說這次地震並不危險，但她提醒觀眾準備緊急避難包。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A44","t":"地震學家"},{"w":"Richter scale","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a scale that measures the strength of an earthquake","cn":"芮氏規模","s":"The earthquake measured 6.5 on the ______ ______, so the government sent rescue teams to the area immediately.","zh":"那場地震在芮氏規模上達到6.5級，所以政府立即派遣救援隊前往該地區。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A45","t":"芮氏規模"},{"w":"fault zone","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an area with many cracks where rocks move","cn":"斷層帶","s":"The town lies inside an active ______ ______, so all new buildings there must follow strict safety rules.","zh":"這座城鎮位於一個活躍的斷層帶內，所以那裡所有新建築都必須遵守嚴格的安全規定。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A46","t":"斷層帶"},{"w":"shockwave","pos":"n.","def":"a strong wave of energy that travels through the ground or air","cn":"震波","s":"The ________ from the earthquake travelled hundreds of kilometres, and people in the capital felt their buildings sway.","zh":"地震產生的震波傳遞了數百公里，而首都的人們感覺到他們的建築物在搖晃。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A47","t":"震波"},{"w":"liquefaction","pos":"n.","def":"when shaken wet soil starts to behave like a liquid","cn":"土壤液化","s":"________ made several buildings sink into the ground, because the soil near the river was full of water.","zh":"土壤液化讓好幾棟建築物陷入地下，因為河邊的土壤充滿了水。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A48","t":"土壤液化"},{"w":"rupture","pos":"v.","def":"to break or burst suddenly","cn":"破裂","s":"When the rocks along the fault suddenly ________, huge amounts of energy are released, and the ground begins to shake.","zh":"當斷層沿線的岩石突然破裂時，大量能量被釋放出來，地面就開始搖晃。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A49","t":"破裂"},{"w":"quake","pos":"n.","def":"an informal word for an earthquake","cn":"地震（口語）","s":"The ________ was short, but it knocked books off the shelves, so the library closed early to clean up.","zh":"那場地震很短暫，但它把書從書架上震落，所以圖書館提早關門整理。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A50","t":"地震"},{"w":"volcanologist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies volcanoes","cn":"火山學家","s":"The ________ wore a special suit near the lava, because the heat was strong enough to burn normal clothes.","zh":"那位火山學家在熔岩附近穿著特殊防護衣，因為那裡的高溫足以燒毀一般衣物。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A51","t":"火山學家"},{"w":"Ring of Fire","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the area around the Pacific Ocean with many volcanoes and earthquakes","cn":"環太平洋火山帶","s":"Taiwan is part of the ______ ______ ______, so we experience many earthquakes, and we also enjoy many hot springs.","zh":"臺灣是環太平洋火山帶的一部分，所以我們經歷許多地震，而且我們也享有許多溫泉。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A52","t":"環太平洋火山帶"},{"w":"sinkhole","pos":"n.","def":"a hole that suddenly opens in the ground","cn":"天坑；地陷","s":"A huge ________ opened in the middle of the road after heavy rain, so the police closed the street for several days.","zh":"大雨過後，道路中央突然出現一個巨大的天坑，所以警方封閉了那條街好幾天。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A53","t":"天坑"},{"w":"evacuation drill","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a practice of leaving a building quickly in an emergency","cn":"疏散演練","s":"Our school holds an ______ ______ every September, and students learn to leave the building calmly in under three minutes.","zh":"我們學校每年九月都會舉行疏散演練，而學生學習在三分鐘內冷靜地離開大樓。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A54","t":"疏散演練"},{"w":"active volcano","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a volcano that has erupted recently or may erupt soon","cn":"活火山","s":"Iceland has many ______ ______, but tourists still visit them because the views are amazing and the guides are well trained.","zh":"冰島有許多活火山，但遊客仍然去參觀，因為景色壯觀而且導遊訓練有素。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A55","t":"活火山"},{"w":"extinct volcano","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a volcano that will never erupt again","cn":"死火山","s":"Edinburgh Castle stands on an ______ ______, so visitors can enjoy the view without worrying about an eruption.","zh":"愛丁堡城堡矗立在一座死火山上，所以遊客可以欣賞美景而不必擔心火山噴發。","part":"A","sec":"Volcanoes & Earthquakes 火山與地震","lab":"A56","t":"死火山"},{"w":"igneous rock","pos":"n.phr.","def":"rock formed when hot melted rock cools","cn":"火成岩","s":"Basalt is a common ______ ______, and it forms when lava cools quickly on the surface of the Earth.","zh":"玄武岩是一種常見的火成岩，而它是在熔岩於地表迅速冷卻時形成的。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A57","t":"火成岩"},{"w":"sedimentary rock","pos":"n.phr.","def":"rock made from layers of sand, mud or shells pressed together","cn":"沉積岩","s":"______ ______ often contains fossils, so it is the best place to look for clues about ancient life.","zh":"沉積岩經常含有化石，所以它是尋找古代生物線索的最佳地方。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A58","t":"沉積岩"},{"w":"metamorphic rock","pos":"n.phr.","def":"rock changed by heat and pressure","cn":"變質岩","s":"Marble is a ______ ______ that forms deep underground, and artists have used it for statues for thousands of years.","zh":"大理石是一種在地底深處形成的變質岩，而藝術家數千年來一直用它來製作雕像。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A59","t":"變質岩"},{"w":"granite","pos":"n.","def":"a very hard grey or pink rock","cn":"花崗岩","s":"The kitchen counter is made of ________, so it does not scratch easily, and it stays cool even in summer.","zh":"廚房流理臺是花崗岩做的，所以它不容易刮傷，而且即使在夏天也保持涼爽。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A60","t":"花崗岩"},{"w":"basalt","pos":"n.","def":"a dark rock formed from cooled lava","cn":"玄武岩","s":"The islands of Penghu are famous for their ________ columns, and many tourists take photos of these unusual rock shapes.","zh":"澎湖群島以玄武岩柱聞名，而許多遊客會拍下這些奇特岩石形狀的照片。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A61","t":"玄武岩"},{"w":"marble","pos":"n.","def":"a smooth hard stone often used in buildings and statues","cn":"大理石","s":"Taroko Gorge has walls of white ________, and the river has cut through the stone for millions of years.","zh":"太魯閣峽谷有白色大理石構成的峭壁，而河流已經切穿這些石頭數百萬年。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A62","t":"大理石"},{"w":"sandstone","pos":"n.","def":"rock made of sand pressed together","cn":"砂岩","s":"The cliffs along the coast are made of soft ________, so the wind and waves have carved them into strange shapes.","zh":"海岸沿線的懸崖是由鬆軟的砂岩構成，所以風和海浪把它們雕刻成奇特的形狀。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A63","t":"砂岩"},{"w":"quartz","pos":"n.","def":"a hard clear or white mineral","cn":"石英","s":"My little brother found a shiny piece of ________ on the beach, and he keeps it in a box with his other treasures.","zh":"我弟弟在海灘上發現一塊閃亮的石英，而他把它和其他寶物一起收在盒子裡。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A64","t":"石英"},{"w":"crystal","pos":"n.","def":"a solid with a regular shape and flat sides","cn":"晶體；水晶","s":"Salt forms tiny ________ when seawater dries, and you can see their square shapes with a simple magnifying glass.","zh":"海水乾掉時鹽會形成微小的晶體，而你可以用簡單的放大鏡看到它們的方形結構。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A65","t":"晶體"},{"w":"gemstone","pos":"n.","def":"a valuable stone used in jewellery","cn":"寶石","s":"A ruby is a red ________ that forms deep underground, but it becomes beautiful only after it is cut and polished.","zh":"紅寶石是一種在地底深處形成的紅色寶石，但它要經過切割和拋光後才會變得美麗。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A66","t":"寶石"},{"w":"rock cycle","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the slow process in which rocks change from one type to another","cn":"岩石循環","s":"The ______ ______ never stops, because rocks are always being broken down, buried, heated and pushed up again.","zh":"岩石循環從不停止，因為岩石總是不斷被分解、掩埋、加熱，然後再次被推升上來。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A67","t":"岩石循環"},{"w":"weathering","pos":"n.","def":"the breaking down of rock by weather, water or plants","cn":"風化作用","s":"Years of ________ have made the old stone steps smooth, and some of the carvings are now hard to see.","zh":"多年的風化作用讓那些古老的石階變得光滑，而有些雕刻現在已經很難看清楚了。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A68","t":"風化作用"},{"w":"canyon","pos":"n.","def":"a deep valley with steep sides, usually cut by a river","cn":"峽谷","s":"The Grand ________ is over a kilometre deep, and it took the Colorado River millions of years to carve it.","zh":"大峽谷深達一公里以上，而科羅拉多河花了數百萬年才把它切割出來。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A69","t":"峽谷"},{"w":"gorge","pos":"n.","def":"a narrow valley with steep rocky walls","cn":"峽谷；山峽","s":"We walked along the narrow ________ all morning, but we had to wear helmets because small rocks sometimes fell from above.","zh":"我們整個早上沿著狹窄的峽谷行走，但我們必須戴安全帽，因為有時會有小石頭從上方掉落。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A70","t":"峽谷"},{"w":"valley","pos":"n.","def":"low land between hills or mountains","cn":"山谷","s":"The village lies in a green ________ between two mountains, so it is cool in summer but very foggy in winter.","zh":"那座村莊位於兩座山之間的翠綠山谷中，所以夏天涼爽，但冬天霧很濃。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A71","t":"山谷"},{"w":"mountain range","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a long line of mountains","cn":"山脈","s":"The Central ______ ______ divides Taiwan into east and west, and it has more than two hundred peaks over 3,000 metres.","zh":"中央山脈把臺灣分成東西兩半，而且它有兩百多座超過三千公尺的山峰。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A72","t":"山脈"},{"w":"peak","pos":"n.","def":"the pointed top of a mountain","cn":"山峰","s":"We reached the ________ just before sunrise, and the view of the sea of clouds made the hard climb worthwhile.","zh":"我們在日出前抵達山峰，而雲海的景色讓艱辛的攀登變得值得。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A73","t":"山峰"},{"w":"slope","pos":"n.","def":"ground that goes up or down at an angle","cn":"斜坡","s":"Heavy rain made the ________ above the road unstable, so workers built a strong wall to stop rocks from falling.","zh":"大雨讓道路上方的斜坡變得不穩，所以工人建造了一道堅固的牆來阻止落石。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A74","t":"斜坡"},{"w":"stalactite","pos":"n.","def":"a rock shape that hangs down from the roof of a cave","cn":"鐘乳石","s":"A single ________ can take thousands of years to grow, so visitors are told never to touch the ones in the cave.","zh":"一根鐘乳石可能需要數千年才能長成，所以遊客被告知絕對不要觸摸洞穴裡的鐘乳石。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A75","t":"鐘乳石"},{"w":"stalagmite","pos":"n.","def":"a rock shape that grows up from the floor of a cave","cn":"石筍","s":"Water dripping from the ceiling slowly formed a tall ________ on the floor, and it now looks like a stone tower.","zh":"從洞頂滴下的水在地面上慢慢形成一根高高的石筍，而它現在看起來像一座石塔。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A76","t":"石筍"},{"w":"cavern","pos":"n.","def":"a large cave","cn":"大洞穴","s":"The guide led us into a huge underground ________, and our voices echoed loudly when we spoke.","zh":"導遊帶領我們進入一個巨大的地下洞穴，而我們說話時聲音回響得很大聲。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A77","t":"洞穴"},{"w":"outcrop","pos":"n.","def":"a large rock that sticks out of the ground","cn":"露頭；突出的岩層","s":"We stopped for lunch on a rocky ________ above the river, and from there we could see the whole valley.","zh":"我們在河流上方一塊突出的岩石上停下來吃午餐，而從那裡我們可以看到整個山谷。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A78","t":"岩石"},{"w":"landform","pos":"n.","def":"a natural shape on the Earth's surface, such as a hill","cn":"地形","s":"A delta is a ________ that forms where a river meets the sea, and it often has very rich soil for farming.","zh":"三角洲是一種在河流入海處形成的地形，而它通常擁有非常適合耕種的肥沃土壤。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A79","t":"地形"},{"w":"glacial","pos":"adj.","def":"made or caused by glaciers","cn":"冰河的","s":"The lake was formed by ________ ice thousands of years ago, so its water is very cold and clear even in summer.","zh":"這座湖是在數千年前由冰河冰所形成的，所以即使在夏天湖水也非常冰冷清澈。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A80","t":"冰河"},{"w":"moraine","pos":"n.","def":"a pile of rocks and soil left by a glacier","cn":"冰磧","s":"The hikers crossed a long ________ of loose stones, and the guide explained that a glacier had pushed them there long ago.","zh":"健行者穿越一長片鬆散石頭構成的冰磧，而導遊解釋說很久以前是冰河把它們推到那裡的。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A81","t":"冰磧"},{"w":"geode","pos":"n.","def":"a plain-looking rock with crystals inside","cn":"晶洞","s":"The ________ looked like an ordinary grey stone, but when my dad cut it open, it was full of purple crystals.","zh":"那顆晶洞看起來像一塊普通的灰色石頭，但當我爸爸把它切開時，裡面全是紫色的晶體。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A82","t":"晶洞"},{"w":"ravine","pos":"n.","def":"a deep narrow valley with steep sides","cn":"深谷；溝壑","s":"The bridge crosses a deep ________, so some visitors feel nervous when they look down at the river below.","zh":"這座橋橫跨一道很深的溝壑，所以有些遊客往下看到河流時會感到緊張。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A83","t":"溝壑"},{"w":"rock formation","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a natural shape made of rock","cn":"岩石地形；奇岩","s":"The famous Queen's Head at Yehliu is a ______ ______, but scientists worry that it may break because of weathering.","zh":"野柳著名的女王頭是一個岩石地形，但科學家擔心它可能會因為風化而斷裂。","part":"A","sec":"Rocks, Minerals & Landforms 岩石、礦物與地形","lab":"A84","t":"岩石地形"},{"w":"tributary","pos":"n.","def":"a small river that flows into a bigger river","cn":"支流","s":"The small stream behind our school is a ________ of the Tamsui River, so rubbish thrown into it can end up in the sea.","zh":"我們學校後面的小溪是淡水河的一條支流，所以丟進去的垃圾最後可能會流到海裡。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A85","t":"支流"},{"w":"meander","pos":"v.","def":"to follow a slow, winding course","cn":"蜿蜒流動","s":"The river ________ through the flat farmland, so it takes much longer to reach the sea than a straight river would.","zh":"那條河蜿蜒流過平坦的農田，所以它流到海的時間比一條筆直的河長得多。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A86","t":"蜿蜒流"},{"w":"floodplain","pos":"n.","def":"flat land next to a river that floods sometimes","cn":"氾濫平原","s":"Farmers like the ________ because the soil is very rich, but their fields are often covered with water after typhoons.","zh":"農民喜歡氾濫平原，因為那裡的土壤非常肥沃，但颱風過後他們的田地常常被水淹沒。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A87","t":"氾濫平原"},{"w":"waterfall","pos":"n.","def":"water falling from a high place, such as a cliff","cn":"瀑布","s":"We could hear the ________ long before we saw it, and the cold spray felt wonderful on such a hot day.","zh":"我們在看到瀑布之前很久就聽到了它的聲音，而在那麼熱的天氣裡，冰涼的水霧讓人覺得很舒服。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A88","t":"瀑布"},{"w":"rapids","pos":"n.","def":"part of a river where water flows fast over rocks","cn":"急流","s":"Our raft bounced wildly through the ________, and everyone screamed and laughed at the same time.","zh":"我們的橡皮艇在急流中劇烈顛簸，而每個人都同時尖叫又大笑。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A89","t":"急流"},{"w":"oxbow lake","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a curved lake formed when a river changes its course","cn":"牛軛湖","s":"Over many years, the river changed direction and left behind an ______ ______, which is now a home for many birds.","zh":"經過許多年，河流改變了方向，留下了一座牛軛湖，而它現在是許多鳥類的家。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A90","t":"牛軛湖"},{"w":"hydrology","pos":"n.","def":"the study of water on and under the Earth's surface","cn":"水文學","s":"Experts in ________ studied the river for years, so they could warn the city before dangerous floods arrived.","zh":"水文學專家研究這條河流多年，所以他們能在危險的洪水來臨前向城市發出警告。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A91","t":"水文學"},{"w":"river mouth","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the place where a river flows into the sea","cn":"河口","s":"Many birds gather at the ______ ______ in winter, because the water there is full of small fish and crabs.","zh":"許多鳥類冬天聚集在河口，因為那裡的水域充滿小魚和螃蟹。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A92","t":"河口"},{"w":"geologic time scale","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a system that divides Earth's long history into periods","cn":"地質年代表","s":"The ______ ______ ______ shows that humans appeared very recently, while dinosaurs lived for more than 160 million years.","zh":"地質年代表顯示人類出現得非常晚，而恐龍則存活了超過一億六千萬年。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A93","t":"地質年代表"},{"w":"billion","pos":"n.","def":"the number 1,000,000,000","cn":"十億","s":"Scientists believe the Earth is about 4.5 ________ years old, but life on land appeared much later than life in the sea.","zh":"科學家相信地球大約有四十五億年歷史，但陸地上的生命出現得比海洋生命晚得多。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A94","t":"億"},{"w":"fossil record","pos":"n.phr.","def":"all the fossils found and what they tell us about past life","cn":"化石紀錄","s":"The ______ ______ is incomplete, because soft animals rarely leave fossils, so scientists still have many unanswered questions.","zh":"化石紀錄並不完整，因為軟體動物很少留下化石，所以科學家仍有許多未解的問題。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A95","t":"化石紀錄"},{"w":"mass extinction","pos":"n.phr.","def":"when a very large number of species die out in a short time","cn":"大滅絕","s":"A ______ ______ happened about 66 million years ago, and most scientists think a giant space rock caused it.","zh":"大約六千六百萬年前發生了一次大滅絕，而大多數科學家認為是一顆巨大的太空岩石造成的。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A96","t":"大滅絕"},{"w":"dinosaur","pos":"n.","def":"a large reptile that lived millions of years ago","cn":"恐龍","s":"My nephew loves every ________ in the museum, and he can name more kinds than most adults can.","zh":"我的姪子喜愛博物館裡的每一隻恐龍，而且他能說出的種類比大多數大人還多。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A97","t":"恐龍"},{"w":"asteroid impact","pos":"n.phr.","def":"when a space rock hits a planet","cn":"小行星撞擊","s":"The huge ______ ______ threw dust into the sky and blocked sunlight, so many plants and animals could not survive.","zh":"那次巨大的小行星撞擊把塵埃拋向天空並遮蔽陽光，所以許多動植物無法存活。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A98","t":"小行星撞擊"},{"w":"meteorite","pos":"n.","def":"a piece of rock from space that lands on Earth","cn":"隕石","s":"The museum lets visitors touch a real ________, and children are amazed that it travelled through space for millions of years.","zh":"博物館讓參觀者觸摸一顆真正的隕石，而孩子們很驚訝它在太空中旅行了數百萬年。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A99","t":"隕石"},{"w":"glaciation","pos":"n.","def":"a time when large areas are covered by ice","cn":"冰河作用；冰川期","s":"The last ________ shaped many valleys in Europe, and the ice left behind lakes that people still visit today.","zh":"最近一次冰河作用塑造了歐洲的許多山谷，而冰留下的湖泊至今仍有人去造訪。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A100","t":"冰河作用"},{"w":"landmass","pos":"n.","def":"a large area of land, such as a continent","cn":"陸塊","s":"Australia is the smallest continental ________, but it still has deserts, rainforests and snowy mountains.","zh":"澳洲是最小的大陸陸塊，但它仍然擁有沙漠、雨林和積雪的山脈。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A101","t":"陸塊"},{"w":"topography","pos":"n.","def":"the shape and height of the land in an area","cn":"地形（起伏）","s":"Taiwan's ________ is very steep, so rivers flow quickly to the sea, and heavy rain often causes landslides.","zh":"臺灣的地形非常陡峭，所以河流很快就流入大海，而且大雨常常造成山崩。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A102","t":"地形"},{"w":"topographic map","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a map that shows the height and shape of the land","cn":"地形圖","s":"Before the hike, our leader studied a ______ ______ carefully, because she wanted to avoid the steepest parts of the trail.","zh":"健行前，我們的領隊仔細研究了一張地形圖，因為她想避開步道最陡的部分。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A103","t":"地形圖"},{"w":"riverbed","pos":"n.","def":"the ground at the bottom of a river","cn":"河床","s":"The ________ was completely dry after months without rain, so the children walked across it and collected smooth stones.","zh":"好幾個月沒下雨後，河床完全乾涸了，所以孩子們走過河床並撿拾光滑的石頭。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A104","t":"河床"},{"w":"water cycle","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the movement of water between the sea, air and land","cn":"水循環","s":"In the ______ ______, water rises from the ocean as vapour, and it later falls back to the ground as rain.","zh":"在水循環中，水以水蒸氣的形式從海洋上升，之後又以雨的形式落回地面。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A105","t":"水循環"},{"w":"ice core","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a long tube of ice drilled out to study the past","cn":"冰芯","s":"Each ______ ______ holds tiny air bubbles from long ago, so scientists can learn what the air was like thousands of years ago.","zh":"每一根冰芯都含有很久以前的微小氣泡，所以科學家可以了解數千年前的空氣是什麼樣子。","part":"A","sec":"Rivers, Landscapes & Deep Time 河流、地貌與地質年代","lab":"A106","t":"冰芯"},{"w":"solar system","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the sun and all the planets and objects that go around it","cn":"太陽系","s":"Our ______ ______ has eight planets, but scientists keep discovering new moons and small icy worlds at its edge.","zh":"我們的太陽系有八顆行星，但科學家不斷在它的邊緣發現新的衛星和冰冷的小天體。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A107","t":"太陽系"},{"w":"planet","pos":"n.","def":"a large round object that moves around a star","cn":"行星","s":"Earth is the only ________ that we know has life, so scientists are excited whenever they find water somewhere else.","zh":"地球是我們所知唯一有生命的行星，所以每當科學家在其他地方發現水時都會很興奮。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A108","t":"行星"},{"w":"planetary","pos":"adj.","def":"related to planets","cn":"行星的","s":"She works as a ________ scientist, and her team studies the weather on Mars to prepare for future human visits.","zh":"她是一名行星科學家，而她的團隊研究火星上的天氣，為未來人類登陸做準備。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A109","t":"行星"},{"w":"orbit","pos":"v.","def":"to move around a planet or star in a curved path","cn":"繞軌道運行","s":"The International Space Station ________ the Earth about sixteen times a day, so the astronauts see many sunrises.","zh":"國際太空站每天繞地球運行大約十六圈，所以太空人能看到許多次日出。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A110","t":"繞 運行"},{"w":"orbital","pos":"adj.","def":"related to the path of an object around a planet or star","cn":"軌道的","s":"Mars has a longer ________ path than Earth, so one year on Mars lasts almost twice as long as ours.","zh":"火星的軌道路徑比地球長，所以火星上的一年幾乎是我們的兩倍長。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A111","t":"軌道"},{"w":"Venus","pos":"n.","def":"the second planet from the sun, very hot and cloudy","cn":"金星","s":"________ is often called Earth's sister planet because of its size, but its surface is hot enough to melt lead.","zh":"金星因為大小相近常被稱為地球的姊妹星，但它的表面熱到足以熔化鉛。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A112","t":"金星"},{"w":"Mars","pos":"n.","def":"the red planet, fourth from the sun","cn":"火星","s":"Several countries have sent robots to ________, and some companies hope to send people there within the next twenty years.","zh":"好幾個國家已經送機器人到火星，而有些公司希望在未來二十年內把人送到那裡。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A113","t":"火星"},{"w":"Jupiter","pos":"n.","def":"the largest planet in our solar system","cn":"木星","s":"________ is so big that all the other planets could fit inside it, and it has a giant storm that has lasted for centuries.","zh":"木星大到其他所有行星都能裝進去，而且它有一個已經持續了好幾個世紀的巨大風暴。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A114","t":"木星"},{"w":"Saturn","pos":"n.","def":"the sixth planet, famous for its rings","cn":"土星","s":"Through the telescope we could clearly see ________ and its beautiful rings, so everyone in the class wanted another look.","zh":"透過望遠鏡我們能清楚看到土星和它美麗的光環，所以班上每個人都想再看一次。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A115","t":"土星"},{"w":"Neptune","pos":"n.","def":"the eighth and farthest planet from the sun","cn":"海王星","s":"________ is so far away that sunlight takes about four hours to reach it, and its winds are the fastest in the solar system.","zh":"海王星遠到陽光要大約四小時才能抵達，而且它的風速是太陽系中最快的。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A116","t":"海王星"},{"w":"dwarf planet","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a small round object that orbits the sun but is not a full planet","cn":"矮行星","s":"Pluto is now called a ______ ______, but many people still think of it as the ninth planet because they learned that at school.","zh":"冥王星現在被稱為矮行星，但許多人仍然把它當成第九顆行星，因為他們在學校是這樣學的。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A117","t":"矮行星"},{"w":"Pluto","pos":"n.","def":"a small icy dwarf planet far from the sun","cn":"冥王星","s":"A spacecraft flew past ________ in 2015, and its photos showed a giant heart-shaped area of ice on the surface.","zh":"一艘太空船在2015年飛越冥王星，而它拍的照片顯示表面上有一大片心形的冰原。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A118","t":"冥王星"},{"w":"moon","pos":"n.","def":"a natural object that moves around a planet","cn":"衛星；月球","s":"Jupiter has dozens of ________, and scientists think one of them may hide a salty ocean under its icy surface.","zh":"木星有數十顆衛星，而科學家認為其中一顆可能在冰冷表面下藏著一片鹹水海洋。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A119","t":"衛星"},{"w":"lunar","pos":"adj.","def":"related to the moon","cn":"月球的；陰曆的","s":"Many Asian festivals follow the ________ calendar, so the date of Chinese New Year changes every year.","zh":"許多亞洲節慶依循陰曆，所以農曆新年的日期每年都不一樣。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A120","t":"陰"},{"w":"crescent","pos":"n.","def":"the curved shape of the moon when only a thin part is lit","cn":"新月形；彎月","s":"A thin ________ appeared in the western sky after sunset, and my grandmother said it looked like a smile.","zh":"日落後西方天空出現一彎細細的新月，而我奶奶說它看起來像一個微笑。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A121","t":"新月"},{"w":"full moon","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the moon when it looks completely round and bright","cn":"滿月","s":"Families in Taiwan eat mooncakes under the ______ ______ during the Mid-Autumn Festival, and many also have barbecues outdoors.","zh":"臺灣的家庭在中秋節時於滿月下吃月餅，而且許多人也會在戶外烤肉。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A122","t":"滿月"},{"w":"solar eclipse","pos":"n.phr.","def":"when the moon blocks the sun's light from Earth","cn":"日蝕","s":"We watched the ______ ______ through special glasses, because looking directly at the sun can damage your eyes.","zh":"我們透過特殊眼鏡觀看日蝕，因為直視太陽會傷害眼睛。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A123","t":"日蝕"},{"w":"lunar eclipse","pos":"n.phr.","def":"when the Earth's shadow falls on the moon","cn":"月蝕","s":"During the ______ ______, the moon turned a dark red colour, so people called it a \"blood moon\" on social media.","zh":"月蝕期間，月亮變成暗紅色，所以人們在社群媒體上稱它為「血月」。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A124","t":"月蝕"},{"w":"asteroid","pos":"n.","def":"a large rock that moves around the sun","cn":"小行星","s":"Scientists track every large ________ near Earth, so they would have years of warning if one were heading toward us.","zh":"科學家追蹤地球附近每一顆大型小行星，所以如果有一顆朝我們飛來，他們會提前好幾年得到警告。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A125","t":"小行星"},{"w":"asteroid belt","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the area between Mars and Jupiter with many asteroids","cn":"小行星帶","s":"The ______ ______ lies between Mars and Jupiter, but the rocks are so far apart that spacecraft can pass through safely.","zh":"小行星帶位於火星和木星之間，但那些岩石彼此相距非常遠，所以太空船可以安全通過。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A126","t":"小行星帶"},{"w":"comet","pos":"n.","def":"an icy object with a bright tail that travels around the sun","cn":"彗星","s":"Halley's ________ returns about every 76 years, so most people can see it only once in their lifetime.","zh":"哈雷彗星大約每七十六年回來一次，所以大多數人一生中只能看到它一次。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A127","t":"彗星"},{"w":"meteor","pos":"n.","def":"a piece of space rock that burns up in the sky","cn":"流星","s":"A bright ________ flashed across the sky while we were camping, and everyone quickly made a wish.","zh":"我們露營時一顆明亮的流星劃過天空，而每個人都趕快許了願。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A128","t":"流星"},{"w":"meteor shower","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a time when many meteors can be seen in the sky","cn":"流星雨","s":"We drove up the mountain to watch the ______ ______, because the city lights make it hard to see anything at home.","zh":"我們開車上山去看流星雨，因為城市的燈光讓我們在家裡很難看到任何東西。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A129","t":"流星雨"},{"w":"shooting star","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an everyday name for a meteor","cn":"流星（口語）","s":"My little sister saw her first ______ ______ last night, and she still will not tell anyone what she wished for.","zh":"我妹妹昨晚看到她人生的第一顆流星，而她到現在仍不肯告訴任何人她許了什麼願。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A130","t":"流星"},{"w":"rotation","pos":"n.","def":"the act of spinning around a centre","cn":"自轉","s":"The Earth's ________ gives us day and night, and one complete turn takes about twenty-four hours.","zh":"地球的自轉帶給我們白天和黑夜，而轉一整圈大約需要二十四小時。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A131","t":"自轉"},{"w":"axis","pos":"n.","def":"an imaginary line that a planet spins around","cn":"地軸；軸","s":"The Earth's ________ is tilted, so different parts of the world receive more sunlight at different times of the year.","zh":"地球的地軸是傾斜的，所以世界上不同地區在一年中不同時間接收到較多的陽光。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A132","t":"地軸"},{"w":"equator","pos":"n.","def":"an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth","cn":"赤道","s":"Countries near the ________ are hot all year round, and they usually have only a wet season and a dry season.","zh":"靠近赤道的國家一年到頭都很熱，而且它們通常只有雨季和乾季。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A133","t":"赤道"},{"w":"gas giant","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a huge planet made mostly of gas","cn":"氣態巨行星","s":"Jupiter is a ______ ______, so a spacecraft could never land on it, because it has no solid surface.","zh":"木星是一顆氣態巨行星，所以太空船永遠無法在上面降落，因為它沒有固體表面。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A134","t":"氣態巨行星"},{"w":"rocky planet","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a planet with a hard surface made of rock and metal","cn":"岩質行星","s":"Earth is a ______ ______ like Mars, but our thick atmosphere and liquid water make it much friendlier to life.","zh":"地球和火星一樣是岩質行星，但我們厚厚的大氣層和液態水讓它對生命友善得多。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A135","t":"岩質行星"},{"w":"sunspot","pos":"n.","def":"a dark, cooler area on the surface of the sun","cn":"太陽黑子","s":"Each ________ looks small in photos, but many of them are actually larger than the whole Earth.","zh":"每個太陽黑子在照片中看起來很小，但其中許多其實比整個地球還大。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A136","t":"太陽黑子"},{"w":"solar flare","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a sudden burst of energy from the sun","cn":"太陽閃焰","s":"A strong ______ ______ can disturb radio signals, so airlines sometimes change their routes when one is expected.","zh":"強烈的太陽閃焰會干擾無線電訊號，所以預期會發生時，航空公司有時會更改航線。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A137","t":"太陽閃焰"},{"w":"solar wind","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a stream of particles flowing out from the sun","cn":"太陽風","s":"The ______ ______ never stops blowing, but the Earth's magnetic field protects us from most of its harmful particles.","zh":"太陽風從未停止吹拂，但地球的磁場保護我們免受其中大部分有害粒子的傷害。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A138","t":"太陽風"},{"w":"aurora","pos":"n.","def":"colourful lights in the night sky near the poles","cn":"極光","s":"We travelled to northern Norway to see the ________, and the green lights dancing across the sky were unforgettable.","zh":"我們到挪威北部去看極光，而在天空中舞動的綠色光芒令人難忘。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A139","t":"極光"},{"w":"Kuiper Belt","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an area of icy objects beyond Neptune","cn":"古柏帶","s":"Pluto lives in the ______ ______, which is a cold region full of icy objects, so it is very hard to study.","zh":"冥王星位於古柏帶，那是一個充滿冰冷天體的寒冷區域，所以很難研究。","part":"A","sec":"The Solar System 太陽系","lab":"A140","t":"古柏帶"},{"w":"star","pos":"n.","def":"a huge ball of burning gas in space, like the sun","cn":"恆星","s":"The sun is actually an ordinary ________, but it looks much bigger and brighter because it is so close to us.","zh":"太陽其實是一顆普通的恆星，但因為它離我們非常近，所以看起來大得多也亮得多。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A141","t":"恆星"},{"w":"galaxy","pos":"n.","def":"a huge group of billions of stars","cn":"星系","s":"Our ________ contains hundreds of billions of stars, and astronomers think there are billions of other galaxies too.","zh":"我們的星系包含數千億顆恆星，而天文學家認為還有數十億個其他星系。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A142","t":"星系"},{"w":"Milky Way","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the galaxy that contains our solar system","cn":"銀河","s":"On a clear night in the mountains, you can see the ______ ______ as a bright band across the sky, but it is invisible in the city.","zh":"在山上晴朗的夜晚，你可以看到銀河像一條明亮的光帶橫跨天空，但在城市裡卻看不見。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A143","t":"銀河"},{"w":"constellation","pos":"n.","def":"a group of stars that forms a pattern","cn":"星座","s":"Orion is an easy ________ to find in winter, because three bright stars form his belt in a straight line.","zh":"獵戶座是冬天很容易找到的星座，因為三顆明亮的星星排成一直線構成他的腰帶。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A144","t":"星座"},{"w":"nebula","pos":"n.","def":"a huge cloud of gas and dust in space","cn":"星雲","s":"New stars are born inside a ________, and space telescopes have taken amazing colourful photos of these clouds.","zh":"新的恆星在星雲中誕生，而太空望遠鏡已經拍下這些雲氣令人驚嘆的彩色照片。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A145","t":"星雲"},{"w":"supernova","pos":"n.","def":"the huge explosion of a dying star","cn":"超新星","s":"When a giant star dies in a ________, it can shine brighter than a whole galaxy for several weeks.","zh":"當一顆巨大的恆星在超新星爆炸中死亡時，它可以在幾週內比整個星系還亮。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A146","t":"超新星"},{"w":"black hole","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an area in space where gravity is so strong that light cannot escape","cn":"黑洞","s":"Nothing can escape from a ______ ______, so scientists could not photograph one directly until 2019.","zh":"沒有任何東西能逃離黑洞，所以科學家直到2019年才能直接拍攝到一個黑洞。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A147","t":"黑洞"},{"w":"neutron star","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a very small, very heavy dead star","cn":"中子星","s":"A ______ ______ is only about twenty kilometres wide, but a single spoonful of it would weigh more than a mountain.","zh":"中子星只有大約二十公里寬，但它的一小匙物質就比一座山還重。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A148","t":"中子星"},{"w":"red giant","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a large, old star that has grown cooler and redder","cn":"紅巨星","s":"In about five billion years, the sun will become a ______ ______, and it may grow big enough to swallow the Earth.","zh":"大約五十億年後，太陽將變成一顆紅巨星，而且它可能會膨脹到足以吞噬地球。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A149","t":"紅巨星"},{"w":"white dwarf","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a small, hot, dense star near the end of its life","cn":"白矮星","s":"After it stops burning fuel, the sun will shrink into a ______ ______, and it will slowly cool down for billions of years.","zh":"停止燃燒燃料後，太陽會縮小成一顆白矮星，而它會在數十億年間慢慢冷卻。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A150","t":"白矮星"},{"w":"light-year","pos":"n.","def":"the distance light travels in one year","cn":"光年","s":"The nearest star is over four ________ away, so even our fastest spacecraft would need thousands of years to get there.","zh":"最近的恆星距離我們超過四光年，所以即使是我們最快的太空船也需要數千年才能抵達。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A151","t":"光年"},{"w":"astronomer","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies stars and planets","cn":"天文學家","s":"The ________ stayed awake all night at the observatory, and she finally spotted the faint comet just before dawn.","zh":"那位天文學家在天文臺整夜沒睡，而她終於在黎明前發現了那顆暗淡的彗星。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A152","t":"天文學家"},{"w":"astrophysics","pos":"n.","def":"the science of how stars and galaxies work","cn":"天體物理學","s":"He wants to study ________ at university, because he has loved reading about black holes since he was a child.","zh":"他想在大學念天體物理學，因為他從小就喜歡閱讀關於黑洞的資料。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A153","t":"天體物理學"},{"w":"cosmos","pos":"n.","def":"the whole universe, seen as an ordered system","cn":"宇宙","s":"Looking at the night sky makes me feel tiny, but it also makes me curious about our place in the ________.","zh":"仰望夜空讓我覺得自己很渺小，但也讓我對我們在宇宙中的位置感到好奇。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A154","t":"宇宙"},{"w":"cosmic","pos":"adj.","def":"related to the universe or outer space","cn":"宇宙的","s":"Astronauts on long missions face ________ rays from space, so engineers design special shields for their spacecraft.","zh":"執行長期任務的太空人會面臨來自太空的宇宙射線，所以工程師為他們的太空船設計特殊的防護罩。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A155","t":"宇宙"},{"w":"universe","pos":"n.","def":"everything that exists, including all stars and space","cn":"宇宙","s":"The ________ is about 13.8 billion years old, and it is still getting bigger every second.","zh":"宇宙大約有一百三十八億年歷史，而且它每一秒都還在變大。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A156","t":"宇宙"},{"w":"Big Bang","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the event that most scientists think started the universe","cn":"大霹靂","s":"Most scientists believe the universe began with the ______ ______, although nobody knows what existed before it.","zh":"大多數科學家相信宇宙起源於大霹靂，雖然沒有人知道在那之前存在著什麼。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A157","t":"大霹靂"},{"w":"dark matter","pos":"n.phr.","def":"invisible material that we know exists because of its gravity","cn":"暗物質","s":"We cannot see ______ ______, but scientists know it is there because it pulls on stars and galaxies.","zh":"我們看不見暗物質，但科學家知道它存在，因為它會拉扯恆星和星系。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A158","t":"暗物質"},{"w":"dark energy","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a mysterious force that makes the universe expand faster","cn":"暗能量","s":"______ ______ is pushing galaxies apart faster and faster, but nobody yet understands what it really is.","zh":"暗能量正把星系推得越來越快地分開，但至今還沒有人了解它到底是什麼。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A159","t":"暗能量"},{"w":"observatory","pos":"n.","def":"a building with large telescopes for watching the sky","cn":"天文臺","s":"The ________ is built on the top of a high mountain, because the air there is clear and there is very little light pollution.","zh":"那座天文臺建在高山頂上，因為那裡空氣清澈而且光害很少。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A160","t":"天文臺"},{"w":"telescope","pos":"n.","def":"a tool that makes faraway objects look closer","cn":"望遠鏡","s":"I got a small ________ for my birthday, and now I go up to the roof every clear night to look at the moon.","zh":"我生日時收到一架小望遠鏡，而現在每個晴朗的夜晚我都會到屋頂上看月亮。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A161","t":"望遠鏡"},{"w":"space telescope","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a telescope that orbits above the Earth's atmosphere","cn":"太空望遠鏡","s":"A ______ ______ takes much clearer pictures than one on the ground, because the air does not blur its view.","zh":"太空望遠鏡拍的照片比地面上的清晰得多，因為空氣不會讓它的視野變模糊。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A162","t":"太空望遠鏡"},{"w":"exoplanet","pos":"n.","def":"a planet that moves around a star other than the sun","cn":"系外行星","s":"Astronomers have found thousands of ________, and a few of them might have the right temperature for liquid water.","zh":"天文學家已經發現了數千顆系外行星，而其中少數可能有適合液態水存在的溫度。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A163","t":"系外行星"},{"w":"habitable zone","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the area around a star where water can stay liquid","cn":"適居帶","s":"Earth lies in the sun's ______ ______, so it is neither too hot nor too cold for oceans to exist.","zh":"地球位於太陽的適居帶內，所以對海洋的存在而言既不太熱也不太冷。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A164","t":"適居帶"},{"w":"interstellar","pos":"adj.","def":"between the stars","cn":"星際的","s":"Two spacecraft launched in the 1970s have now entered ________ space, but they still send weak signals back to Earth.","zh":"1970年代發射的兩艘太空船現在已經進入星際空間，但它們仍然把微弱的訊號傳回地球。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A165","t":"星際"},{"w":"celestial","pos":"adj.","def":"in or related to the sky or outer space","cn":"天體的；天空的","s":"Ancient sailors used ________ objects like the stars to find their way, because they had no maps or GPS.","zh":"古代水手利用星星之類的天體來辨別方向，因為他們沒有地圖或衛星定位。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A166","t":"天"},{"w":"stargazing","pos":"n.","def":"the activity of looking at the stars","cn":"觀星","s":"________ is popular in Hehuanshan, so on weekends many families drive up the mountain with blankets and hot drinks.","zh":"在合歡山觀星很受歡迎，所以每到週末許多家庭會帶著毯子和熱飲開車上山。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A167","t":"觀星"},{"w":"quasar","pos":"n.","def":"an extremely bright and distant object powered by a black hole","cn":"類星體","s":"A ________ can be brighter than a thousand galaxies, but it looks like a faint dot because it is so far away.","zh":"一個類星體可能比一千個星系還亮，但因為它非常遙遠，所以看起來只是一個暗淡的小點。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A168","t":"類星體"},{"w":"radio telescope","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a telescope that collects radio waves from space","cn":"電波望遠鏡","s":"China built a huge ______ ______ in a mountain valley, and it listens for faint signals from distant stars.","zh":"中國在一處山谷中建造了一座巨大的電波望遠鏡，而它聆聽來自遙遠恆星的微弱訊號。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A169","t":"電波望遠鏡"},{"w":"star cluster","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a group of stars that are close together","cn":"星團","s":"The Pleiades is a beautiful ______ ______, and on a dark night you can see six or seven of its stars without a telescope.","zh":"昴宿星團是一個美麗的星團，而在黑暗的夜晚不用望遠鏡就能看到其中六、七顆星。","part":"A","sec":"Stars, Galaxies & the Universe 恆星、星系與宇宙","lab":"A170","t":"星團"},{"w":"space exploration","pos":"n.phr.","def":"travelling into space to learn about it","cn":"太空探索","s":"______ ______ is very expensive, but it has given us many useful inventions, such as better weather forecasts and GPS.","zh":"太空探索非常昂貴，但它為我們帶來許多有用的發明，例如更好的天氣預報和衛星定位。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A171","t":"太空探索"},{"w":"astronaut","pos":"n.","def":"a person trained to travel in space","cn":"太空人","s":"The ________ trained for years before her mission, and she said the hardest part was being away from her family.","zh":"那位太空人在任務前接受了多年訓練，而她說最困難的部分是離開家人。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A172","t":"太空人"},{"w":"spacecraft","pos":"n.","def":"a vehicle that travels in space","cn":"太空船","s":"The ________ took seven months to reach Mars, so engineers had to plan every detail of the journey very carefully.","zh":"那艘太空船花了七個月才抵達火星，所以工程師必須非常仔細地規劃旅程的每個細節。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A173","t":"太空船"},{"w":"space station","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a large spacecraft where people live and work in orbit","cn":"太空站","s":"Astronauts on the ______ ______ grow vegetables in space, and they also do experiments that cannot be done on Earth.","zh":"太空站上的太空人在太空中種植蔬菜，而且他們也進行在地球上無法做的實驗。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A174","t":"太空站"},{"w":"rocket","pos":"n.","def":"a vehicle pushed upward by burning fuel","cn":"火箭","s":"The ________ shook the ground as it rose into the sky, and the crowd cheered until it disappeared into the clouds.","zh":"火箭升空時震動了地面，而群眾一直歡呼直到它消失在雲層中。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A175","t":"火箭"},{"w":"launch pad","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the place from which a rocket takes off","cn":"發射臺","s":"The rocket stood on the ______ ______ for hours, but the launch was cancelled because of strong winds.","zh":"火箭在發射臺上矗立了好幾個小時，但發射因為強風而取消了。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A176","t":"發射臺"},{"w":"countdown","pos":"n.","def":"counting backwards to zero before something starts","cn":"倒數計時","s":"The ________ reached zero and the engines roared, so everyone in the control room held their breath.","zh":"倒數計時歸零、引擎轟鳴，所以控制室裡的每個人都屏住了呼吸。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A177","t":"倒數計時"},{"w":"lift-off","pos":"n.","def":"the moment a rocket leaves the ground","cn":"升空","s":"Just seconds after ________, the rocket was moving faster than a plane, and soon it was only a bright dot in the sky.","zh":"升空後短短幾秒，火箭的速度就比飛機還快，而很快它就只是天空中的一個亮點。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A178","t":"升空"},{"w":"mission control","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the team on Earth that guides a space flight","cn":"任務控制中心","s":"The astronauts talked to ______ ______ every day, and the engineers on the ground helped them fix problems with the equipment.","zh":"太空人每天和任務控制中心通話，而地面上的工程師幫助他們修理設備的問題。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A179","t":"任務控制中心"},{"w":"spacesuit","pos":"n.","def":"special clothing that protects astronauts in space","cn":"太空衣","s":"A ________ is very heavy on Earth, but in space it protects astronauts from extreme heat, cold and radiation.","zh":"太空衣在地球上非常重，但在太空中它保護太空人免受極端的高溫、低溫和輻射傷害。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A180","t":"太空衣"},{"w":"spacewalk","pos":"n.","def":"time an astronaut spends working outside a spacecraft","cn":"太空漫步","s":"During the six-hour ________, the astronauts repaired a solar panel, and millions of people watched the live video online.","zh":"在六小時的太空漫步期間，太空人修理了一片太陽能板，而數百萬人在網路上觀看直播影片。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A181","t":"太空漫步"},{"w":"zero gravity","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a state where things float because they seem to have no weight","cn":"零重力","s":"In ______ ______, water forms floating balls instead of pouring, so astronauts drink through special straws.","zh":"在零重力狀態下，水會形成漂浮的水球而不會倒出來，所以太空人用特殊的吸管喝水。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A182","t":"零重力"},{"w":"weightless","pos":"adj.","def":"having no weight, so you float","cn":"失重的","s":"The astronauts felt ________ as soon as they reached orbit, and their pens and notebooks floated around the cabin.","zh":"太空人一進入軌道就感到失重，而他們的筆和筆記本在艙內四處漂浮。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A183","t":"失重"},{"w":"microgravity","pos":"n.","def":"very weak gravity, like inside an orbiting spacecraft","cn":"微重力","s":"Long stays in ________ make astronauts' bones and muscles weaker, so they must exercise for two hours every day.","zh":"長時間待在微重力環境會讓太空人的骨骼和肌肉變弱，所以他們每天必須運動兩小時。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A184","t":"微重力"},{"w":"re-entry","pos":"n.","def":"the return of a spacecraft into the Earth's atmosphere","cn":"重返大氣層","s":"________ is one of the most dangerous parts of a mission, because the spacecraft becomes extremely hot as it falls through the air.","zh":"重返大氣層是任務中最危險的部分之一，因為太空船穿過空氣墜落時會變得極度灼熱。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A185","t":"重返大氣層"},{"w":"heat shield","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a cover that protects a spacecraft from extreme heat","cn":"隔熱罩","s":"The capsule has a thick ______ ______ on the bottom, so the astronauts inside stay cool while the outside glows red.","zh":"太空艙底部有一層厚厚的隔熱罩，所以外部燒得通紅時，裡面的太空人仍然保持涼爽。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A186","t":"隔熱罩"},{"w":"rover","pos":"n.","def":"a vehicle that drives on the surface of another planet","cn":"探測車","s":"The ________ has been driving across Mars for years, and it sends back photos that look surprisingly like deserts on Earth.","zh":"那輛探測車已經在火星上行駛多年，而它傳回的照片看起來出奇地像地球上的沙漠。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A187","t":"探測車"},{"w":"lander","pos":"n.","def":"a spacecraft designed to land on a planet or moon","cn":"登陸器","s":"The ________ touched down gently on the moon, and the scientists in the control room jumped up and hugged each other.","zh":"登陸器輕輕地降落在月球上，而控制室裡的科學家們跳起來互相擁抱。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A188","t":"登陸器"},{"w":"space probe","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a robot spacecraft sent to explore space","cn":"太空探測器","s":"The ______ ______ has travelled for over forty years, but it is still sending information back to scientists on Earth.","zh":"那個太空探測器已經航行了四十多年，但它仍然把資訊傳回給地球上的科學家。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A189","t":"太空探測器"},{"w":"space agency","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a government organisation that runs space programmes","cn":"太空總署；太空機構","s":"Taiwan's ______ ______ has launched several satellites, and it hopes to train more young engineers in the next ten years.","zh":"臺灣的太空機構已經發射了好幾顆人造衛星，而且它希望在未來十年培育更多年輕工程師。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A190","t":"太空機構"},{"w":"space race","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the competition between countries to explore space first","cn":"太空競賽","s":"During the ______ ______, the USA and the Soviet Union competed fiercely, and both countries spent huge amounts of money.","zh":"在太空競賽期間，美國和蘇聯激烈競爭，而兩國都花費了鉅額資金。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A191","t":"太空競賽"},{"w":"moon landing","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the event of a spacecraft or people landing on the moon","cn":"登月","s":"My grandparents watched the first ______ ______ on a small black-and-white TV, and they still remember that exciting night.","zh":"我的祖父母在一臺小小的黑白電視上看了第一次登月，而他們至今仍記得那個令人興奮的夜晚。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A192","t":"登月"},{"w":"space junk","pos":"n.phr.","def":"old, broken objects left floating in orbit","cn":"太空垃圾","s":"There are millions of pieces of ______ ______ around the Earth, and even a tiny piece can damage a working satellite.","zh":"地球周圍有數百萬片太空垃圾，而即使是很小的一片也能損壞運作中的人造衛星。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A193","t":"太空垃圾"},{"w":"low Earth orbit","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the area of space close above the Earth's atmosphere","cn":"低地球軌道","s":"Most satellites travel in ______ ______ ______, so this area is becoming crowded, and collisions are a growing risk.","zh":"大多數人造衛星在低地球軌道上運行，所以這個區域變得越來越擁擠，而碰撞的風險也日益增加。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A194","t":"低地球軌道"},{"w":"space tourism","pos":"n.phr.","def":"travelling to space for fun as a paying passenger","cn":"太空旅遊","s":"______ ______ is still extremely expensive, but some companies believe ordinary people will be able to afford it one day.","zh":"太空旅遊仍然極其昂貴，但有些公司相信有一天普通人也能負擔得起。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A195","t":"太空旅遊"},{"w":"reusable rocket","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a rocket that can be flown more than once","cn":"可重複使用火箭","s":"A ______ ______ lands back on Earth after each flight, so it greatly reduces the cost of sending satellites into space.","zh":"可重複使用火箭每次飛行後都會降落回地球，所以它大幅降低了發射人造衛星的成本。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A196","t":"可重複使用火箭"},{"w":"thruster","pos":"n.","def":"a small engine used to move or turn a spacecraft","cn":"推進器","s":"One ________ stopped working during the mission, so the team on the ground had to find another way to turn the spacecraft.","zh":"一具推進器在任務中停止運作，所以地面團隊必須找到另一種方法來轉動太空船。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A197","t":"推進器"},{"w":"propulsion","pos":"n.","def":"the force that pushes something forward","cn":"推進力；推進系統","s":"Engineers are testing new kinds of ________ for spacecraft, because chemical rockets are too slow for long journeys.","zh":"工程師正在測試新型的太空船推進系統，因為化學火箭對長途旅行來說太慢了。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A198","t":"推進系統"},{"w":"extraterrestrial","pos":"adj.","def":"coming from outside the Earth","cn":"外星的","s":"Scientists have not found any ________ life yet, but many believe simple living things may exist on other worlds.","zh":"科學家還沒有發現任何外星生命，但許多人相信簡單的生物可能存在於其他星球上。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A199","t":"外星"},{"w":"airlock","pos":"n.","def":"a small sealed room for moving between areas with different air pressure","cn":"氣閘艙","s":"The astronauts waited inside the ________ while the air was pumped out, and then they opened the door to space.","zh":"太空人在氣閘艙裡等待空氣被抽出，然後他們打開了通往太空的門。","part":"A","sec":"Space Exploration & Space Junk 太空探索與太空垃圾","lab":"A200","t":"氣閘艙"},{"w":"approximate","pos":"adj.","def":"close to the exact number but not exact","cn":"大約的","s":"The guide gave us the ________ height of the volcano, but she said the exact number changes slightly after each eruption.","zh":"導遊告訴我們那座火山的大約高度，但她說確切數字在每次噴發後都會略有改變。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B1","t":"大約"},{"w":"coincidental","pos":"adj.","def":"happening by chance, not planned","cn":"巧合的","s":"The two earthquakes happened on the same day, but scientists said it was ________ because they were on different faults.","zh":"兩場地震在同一天發生，但科學家說那是巧合，因為它們位於不同的斷層上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B2","t":"巧合"},{"w":"constrain","pos":"v.","def":"to limit what someone or something can do","cn":"限制；約束","s":"A small budget ________ the team's research, so they could only study one volcano instead of three.","zh":"微薄的預算限制了團隊的研究，所以他們只能研究一座火山，而不是三座。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B3","t":"限制"},{"w":"conversion","pos":"n.","def":"the act of changing something into another form","cn":"轉換","s":"The ________ of sunlight into electricity powers the space station, and the large solar panels are always turned toward the sun.","zh":"將陽光轉換成電力為太空站提供能源，而那些大型太陽能板總是朝向太陽。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B4","t":"轉換"},{"w":"criterion","pos":"n.","def":"a standard used to judge something","cn":"標準；準則","s":"The most important ________ for a new observatory is dark skies, so most are built far from big cities.","zh":"新天文臺最重要的標準是天空要暗，所以大多數天文臺都建在遠離大城市的地方。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B5","t":"標準"},{"w":"deduction","pos":"n.","def":"reaching a conclusion by careful reasoning","cn":"推論","s":"Through careful ________, the detective in the novel found the thief, but readers were still surprised by the ending.","zh":"透過仔細的推論，小說中的偵探找到了小偷，但讀者仍對結局感到驚訝。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B6","t":"推論"},{"w":"demonstrable","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be shown or proved clearly","cn":"可證明的","s":"The new warning system has had a ________ effect on safety, because fewer people were hurt in this year's earthquakes.","zh":"新的預警系統對安全產生了可證明的效果，因為今年的地震中受傷的人變少了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B7","t":"可證明的"},{"w":"deviation","pos":"n.","def":"a change from the usual or expected path","cn":"偏離；偏差","s":"Even a small ________ from the planned route could send the spacecraft into the wrong orbit, so engineers check it constantly.","zh":"即使是與預定路線的微小偏差也可能讓太空船進入錯誤的軌道，所以工程師不斷檢查。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B8","t":"偏差"},{"w":"distinctive","pos":"adj.","def":"easy to recognise because it is special","cn":"獨特的","s":"Saturn has ________ rings that are easy to spot, so it is often the first planet that children learn to recognise.","zh":"土星有容易辨認的獨特光環，所以它常常是孩子們第一個學會認出的行星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B9","t":"獨特"},{"w":"empirically","pos":"adv.","def":"by observation or experiment rather than theory","cn":"以實證方式","s":"The idea sounded strange at first, but scientists tested it ________, and the results showed that it was correct.","zh":"這個想法起初聽起來很奇怪，但科學家以實證方式測試了它，而結果顯示它是正確的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B10","t":"實證方式"},{"w":"expansion","pos":"n.","def":"the process of becoming larger","cn":"擴張；膨脹","s":"The ________ of the universe means that distant galaxies are moving away from us, and they are moving faster every year.","zh":"宇宙的膨脹意味著遙遠的星系正在遠離我們，而且它們每年都移動得更快。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B11","t":"膨脹"},{"w":"formation","pos":"n.","def":"the process by which something is made","cn":"形成","s":"The ________ of a new island near Japan surprised scientists, and they quickly sailed there to study the fresh lava.","zh":"日本附近一座新島嶼的形成讓科學家很驚訝，而他們很快就航行到那裡研究新鮮的熔岩。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B12","t":"形成"},{"w":"hypothesise","pos":"v.","def":"to suggest an idea that can be tested","cn":"提出假設","s":"Some researchers ________ that animals can sense earthquakes early, but nobody has proved this idea yet.","zh":"有些研究者假設動物能提早感知地震，但還沒有人證實這個想法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B13","t":"假設"},{"w":"indication","pos":"n.","def":"a sign that shows something is happening","cn":"跡象","s":"There was no ________ that the volcano would erupt, so the sudden explosion shocked everyone living nearby.","zh":"沒有任何跡象顯示那座火山會噴發，所以突如其來的爆炸讓住在附近的每個人都很震驚。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B14","t":"跡象"},{"w":"infinite","pos":"adj.","def":"without any limit or end","cn":"無限的","s":"Some people believe that space is ________, but others think it must have an edge somewhere.","zh":"有些人相信太空是無限的，但其他人認為它一定在某處有邊界。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B15","t":"無限的"},{"w":"integrate","pos":"v.","def":"to combine things so they work together","cn":"整合","s":"The app ________ earthquake alerts with maps, so users can quickly see the nearest safe place to go.","zh":"這個應用程式把地震警報和地圖整合在一起，所以使用者可以很快看到最近的安全地點。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B16","t":"整合"},{"w":"interact","pos":"v.","def":"to act on or affect each other","cn":"相互作用；互動","s":"The moon and the oceans ________ through gravity, and this is why the sea rises and falls twice a day.","zh":"月球和海洋透過重力相互作用，而這就是海水一天漲落兩次的原因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B17","t":"相互作用"},{"w":"investigation","pos":"n.","def":"a careful study to find the facts","cn":"調查","s":"After the bridge collapsed, an ________ found that the builders had ignored the earthquake rules, so they were fined.","zh":"橋梁倒塌後，一項調查發現建商忽視了防震規定，所以他們被罰款。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B18","t":"調查"},{"w":"invisible","pos":"adj.","def":"impossible to see","cn":"看不見的","s":"Radio waves are ________ to our eyes, but special telescopes can turn them into pictures that we can understand.","zh":"無線電波是我們的眼睛看不見的，但特殊的望遠鏡能把它們轉換成我們能理解的圖像。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B19","t":"看不見的"},{"w":"irregular","pos":"adj.","def":"not having a regular shape or pattern","cn":"不規則的","s":"Most asteroids have an ________ shape, so they look more like potatoes than round planets.","zh":"大多數小行星的形狀不規則，所以它們看起來比較像馬鈴薯而不是圓形的行星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B20","t":"不規則"},{"w":"notable","pos":"adj.","def":"important or interesting enough to be noticed","cn":"值得注意的","s":"The most ________ discovery of the trip was a new crystal cave, and the news soon spread around the world.","zh":"那次旅程最值得注意的發現是一個新的晶洞，而這則新聞很快就傳遍了全世界。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B21","t":"值得注意的"},{"w":"observe","pos":"v.","def":"to watch something carefully","cn":"觀察","s":"Students ________ the moon every night for a month, and they recorded how its shape slowly changed.","zh":"學生們連續一個月每晚觀察月亮，而且他們記錄了月亮的形狀如何慢慢改變。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B22","t":"觀察"},{"w":"occurrence","pos":"n.","def":"something that happens","cn":"發生的事；事件","s":"Earthquakes are a common ________ in Taiwan, so most buildings are designed to sway without falling down.","zh":"地震在臺灣是常見的事，所以大多數建築都設計成會搖晃但不會倒塌。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B23","t":"事"},{"w":"presence","pos":"n.","def":"the fact of being in a place","cn":"存在","s":"The ________ of water on Mars long ago excites scientists, because life usually needs water to survive.","zh":"火星很久以前有水存在這件事讓科學家很興奮，因為生命通常需要水才能存活。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B24","t":"存在"},{"w":"presumably","pos":"adv.","def":"used to say what you think is probably true","cn":"據推測；大概","s":"The ancient lake is now completely dry, so the climate here was ________ much wetter thousands of years ago.","zh":"那座古湖現在完全乾涸了，所以這裡的氣候在數千年前大概潮濕得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B25","t":"大概"},{"w":"validity","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being correct or acceptable","cn":"正確性；有效性","s":"Other scientists questioned the ________ of his results, because nobody else could repeat the experiment.","zh":"其他科學家質疑他的結果的正確性，因為沒有其他人能重複這個實驗。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B26","t":"正確性"},{"w":"abnormal","pos":"adj.","def":"different from what is usual, often in a worrying way","cn":"異常的","s":"The sensors detected ________ gas levels near the crater, so the park closed the hiking trail immediately.","zh":"感測器偵測到火山口附近的氣體濃度異常，所以公園立即封閉了健行步道。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B27","t":"異常"},{"w":"absolute","pos":"adj.","def":"complete and total","cn":"絕對的；完全的","s":"The cave was in ________ darkness when we turned off our torches, and we could not even see our own hands.","zh":"當我們關掉手電筒時，洞穴裡一片完全的黑暗，而我們甚至看不到自己的手。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B28","t":"完全的"},{"w":"accumulation","pos":"n.","def":"a gradual increase in amount","cn":"累積","s":"The ________ of pressure along the fault worries scientists, because it may be released in a sudden large earthquake.","zh":"斷層沿線壓力的累積讓科學家很擔心，因為它可能在一場突然的大地震中釋放出來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B29","t":"累積"},{"w":"adjustment","pos":"n.","def":"a small change made to improve something","cn":"調整","s":"The pilot made a small ________ to the spacecraft's path, and it entered the moon's orbit perfectly.","zh":"駕駛員對太空船的航道做了一個小小的調整，而它完美地進入了月球軌道。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B30","t":"調整"},{"w":"alteration","pos":"n.","def":"a change in something","cn":"改變；修改","s":"The architect made an ________ to the design after the earthquake, so the new building would be much stronger.","zh":"地震後建築師對設計做了修改，讓新建築會堅固得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B31","t":"修改"},{"w":"analytical","pos":"adj.","def":"using careful, logical thinking to examine things","cn":"分析的","s":"Good scientists need strong ________ skills, because they must make sense of huge amounts of data.","zh":"優秀的科學家需要很強的分析能力，因為他們必須理解大量的數據。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B32","t":"分析"},{"w":"annually","pos":"adv.","def":"once every year","cn":"每年","s":"The meteor shower appears ________ in August, so many families plan camping trips to watch it.","zh":"那場流星雨每年八月都會出現，所以許多家庭會計畫露營去觀賞。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B33","t":"每年"},{"w":"characterise","pos":"v.","def":"to be a typical quality of something","cn":"以……為特徵","s":"Steep mountains and short rivers ________ the landscape of Taiwan, so floods can happen very quickly after heavy rain.","zh":"陡峭的山和短促的河流是臺灣地貌的特徵，所以大雨過後洪水可能很快就發生。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B34","t":"特徵"},{"w":"characteristic","pos":"n.","def":"a typical feature or quality","cn":"特徵","s":"One ________ of Mars is its red dust, and this colour comes from rusty iron in the soil.","zh":"火星的一個特徵是它的紅色塵土，而這種顏色來自土壤中生鏽的鐵。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B35","t":"特徵"},{"w":"coherence","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being logical and well organised","cn":"連貫性","s":"Our teacher praised the ________ of my report, because each paragraph led clearly to the next one.","zh":"老師稱讚我報告的連貫性，因為每一段都清楚地銜接到下一段。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B36","t":"連貫性"},{"w":"comparative","pos":"adj.","def":"involving comparing two or more things","cn":"比較的","s":"We did a ________ study of Mars and Earth, and we found that both planets once had rivers and lakes.","zh":"我們做了一項火星與地球的比較研究，而我們發現兩顆行星都曾經有河流和湖泊。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B37","t":"比較"},{"w":"complexity","pos":"n.","def":"the state of having many connected parts","cn":"複雜性","s":"The ________ of the mission was huge, so thousands of engineers worked together for more than ten years.","zh":"這項任務的複雜性非常高，所以數千名工程師合作了十多年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B38","t":"複雜性"},{"w":"computation","pos":"n.","def":"the process of calculating","cn":"計算","s":"Early space missions relied on ________ done by hand, but today powerful computers do the work in seconds.","zh":"早期的太空任務仰賴人工計算，但今天強大的電腦在幾秒鐘內就能完成這些工作。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B39","t":"計算"},{"w":"conception","pos":"n.","def":"an idea or understanding of something","cn":"概念；觀念","s":"Ancient people had a very different ________ of the universe, and many believed the Earth was at its centre.","zh":"古代人對宇宙有著非常不同的觀念，而許多人相信地球位於宇宙中心。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B40","t":"觀念"},{"w":"confirmation","pos":"n.","def":"a statement or proof that something is true","cn":"證實","s":"The team waited for ________ that the lander had arrived safely, and the room exploded with joy when it came.","zh":"團隊等待登陸器安全抵達的證實，而當消息傳來時整個房間充滿了歡呼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B41","t":"證實"},{"w":"considerably","pos":"adv.","def":"much; a lot","cn":"相當地；大大地","s":"The new telescope is ________ more powerful than the old one, so astronomers can now see galaxies that were invisible before.","zh":"新的望遠鏡比舊的強大得多，所以天文學家現在可以看到以前看不見的星系。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B42","t":"強大得多"},{"w":"contradiction","pos":"n.","def":"a situation where two facts cannot both be true","cn":"矛盾","s":"There was a clear ________ between the two reports, so the scientists checked the data again to find the mistake.","zh":"兩份報告之間有明顯的矛盾，所以科學家再次檢查數據以找出錯誤。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B43","t":"矛盾"},{"w":"contribution","pos":"n.","def":"something you give or do to help","cn":"貢獻","s":"Her ________ to earthquake research was huge, and many of today's safety rules are based on her work.","zh":"她對地震研究的貢獻非常大，而今天許多安全規定都是根據她的研究制定的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B44","t":"貢獻"},{"w":"convincing","pos":"adj.","def":"making you believe that something is true","cn":"令人信服的","s":"The photos from the rover were ________ evidence of ancient rivers, so even doubtful scientists changed their minds.","zh":"探測車拍的照片是古代河流存在的令人信服的證據，所以即使是抱持懷疑的科學家也改變了看法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B45","t":"令人信服的"},{"w":"credibility","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being trusted and believed","cn":"可信度","s":"The website lost its ________ after it shared a fake earthquake warning, and many readers stopped visiting it.","zh":"那個網站分享了一則假的地震警報後失去了可信度，而許多讀者不再造訪它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B46","t":"可信度"},{"w":"detectable","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be noticed or found","cn":"可偵測的","s":"The earthquake was so small that it was only ________ by machines, and nobody in the city felt anything.","zh":"那場地震小到只有機器偵測得到，而城市裡沒有人感覺到任何震動。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B47","t":"偵測得到"},{"w":"disposal","pos":"n.","def":"the act of getting rid of something","cn":"處置；處理","s":"The safe ________ of old satellites is a growing problem, because broken ones can crash into working ones.","zh":"舊人造衛星的安全處置是一個日益嚴重的問題，因為損壞的衛星可能撞上運作中的衛星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B48","t":"處置"},{"w":"distribution","pos":"n.","def":"the way something is spread over an area","cn":"分布","s":"The map shows the ________ of volcanoes around the world, and most of them are found along plate boundaries.","zh":"這張地圖顯示世界各地火山的分布，而它們大多位於板塊邊界沿線。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B49","t":"分布"},{"w":"dominance","pos":"n.","def":"the state of being the most powerful","cn":"主導地位；優勢","s":"The USA's ________ in space ended when other countries built their own rockets, so the field is now much more competitive.","zh":"當其他國家建造自己的火箭後，美國在太空領域的主導地位就結束了，所以這個領域現在競爭激烈得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B50","t":"主導地位"},{"w":"dramatic","pos":"adj.","def":"sudden and very noticeable","cn":"劇烈的；戲劇性的","s":"There was a ________ change in the landscape after the eruption, and the green forest turned into a grey desert.","zh":"噴發後地貌發生了劇烈的變化，而翠綠的森林變成了灰色的荒漠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B51","t":"劇烈的"},{"w":"elimination","pos":"n.","def":"the complete removal of something","cn":"消除；清除","s":"The total ________ of space junk is impossible, but scientists are testing nets and magnets to collect some of it.","zh":"完全清除太空垃圾是不可能的，但科學家正在測試用網子和磁鐵收集其中一部分。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B52","t":"清除"},{"w":"equation","pos":"n.","def":"a mathematical statement that two things are equal","cn":"方程式","s":"Einstein's famous ________ is very short, but it changed the way scientists understand energy and matter.","zh":"愛因斯坦著名的方程式非常簡短，但它改變了科學家理解能量和物質的方式。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B53","t":"方程式"},{"w":"essentially","pos":"adv.","def":"basically; in the most important ways","cn":"本質上；基本上","s":"A comet is ________ a dirty snowball, but it grows a long bright tail when it gets close to the sun.","zh":"彗星本質上是一顆髒雪球，但當它接近太陽時會長出一條長長的明亮尾巴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B54","t":"本質上"},{"w":"evaluation","pos":"n.","def":"a careful judgement of how good something is","cn":"評估","s":"After a full ________ of the old school, engineers decided to strengthen its walls before the next big earthquake.","zh":"經過對舊校舍的全面評估後，工程師決定在下一次大地震前加固它的牆壁。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B55","t":"評估"},{"w":"eventual","pos":"adj.","def":"happening at the end of a long process","cn":"最終的","s":"Scientists expect the ________ collapse of the cliff, so they have already moved the walking path further inland.","zh":"科學家預期那座懸崖最終會崩塌，所以他們已經把步道移到更內陸的地方。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B56","t":"最終"},{"w":"evidently","pos":"adv.","def":"clearly; it is easy to see that","cn":"顯然","s":"The rocks were ________ shaped by water, because they were smooth and round like stones in a river.","zh":"這些岩石顯然是被水塑造出來的，因為它們像河裡的石頭一樣光滑渾圓。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B57","t":"顯然"},{"w":"explicitly","pos":"adv.","def":"clearly and directly","cn":"明確地","s":"The signs ________ warn visitors not to leave the path, but some tourists still climb onto the dangerous rocks.","zh":"告示牌明確地警告遊客不要離開步道，但有些遊客仍然爬上危險的岩石。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B58","t":"明確地"},{"w":"exploitation","pos":"n.","def":"using something, sometimes unfairly, for profit","cn":"開採；剝削","s":"The ________ of minerals on the moon may become possible, but many people worry about who will own them.","zh":"開採月球上的礦物可能會變得可行，但許多人擔心誰將擁有它們。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B59","t":"開採"},{"w":"exponentially","pos":"adv.","def":"increasing faster and faster","cn":"呈指數地；急遽地","s":"The number of satellites has grown ________ in recent years, so the sky above us is becoming very crowded.","zh":"近年來人造衛星的數量急遽增加，所以我們頭頂上的天空變得非常擁擠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B60","t":"急遽"},{"w":"extraction","pos":"n.","def":"the process of removing something from the ground","cn":"開採；萃取","s":"The ________ of water from ice on the moon could support future bases, because carrying water from Earth is very expensive.","zh":"從月球上的冰萃取水可以支持未來的基地，因為從地球運水非常昂貴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B61","t":"萃取"},{"w":"identification","pos":"n.","def":"the act of recognising who or what something is","cn":"辨識；鑑定","s":"The ________ of the strange rock took weeks, but experts finally confirmed that it was a meteorite.","zh":"那塊奇怪岩石的鑑定花了好幾週，但專家最後確認它是一顆隕石。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B62","t":"鑑定"},{"w":"indicator","pos":"n.","def":"a sign that shows the state of something","cn":"指標","s":"Rising ground is a key ________ of a coming eruption, so scientists measure it with GPS every day.","zh":"地面隆起是即將噴發的重要指標，所以科學家每天用衛星定位測量它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B63","t":"指標"},{"w":"inference","pos":"n.","def":"a conclusion based on evidence","cn":"推論；推斷","s":"From the shape of the valley, the ________ was that a glacier had once filled it, and later tests proved this correct.","zh":"從山谷的形狀推斷，曾經有冰河填滿它，而後來的測試證明這是正確的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B64","t":"推斷"},{"w":"instability","pos":"n.","def":"the state of being likely to change or fall","cn":"不穩定","s":"The ________ of the slope made the road dangerous, so drivers had to take a much longer route.","zh":"斜坡的不穩定讓那條道路變得危險，所以駕駛人必須繞一條遠得多的路。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B65","t":"不穩定"},{"w":"intensity","pos":"n.","def":"the strength of something","cn":"強度","s":"The ________ of the shaking was strongest near the coast, but buildings in the mountains suffered less damage.","zh":"靠近海岸的搖晃強度最強，但山區的建築受損較少。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B66","t":"強度"},{"w":"interpretation","pos":"n.","def":"an explanation of the meaning of something","cn":"解讀；詮釋","s":"Each scientist had a different ________ of the strange signal, so they agreed to collect more data before deciding.","zh":"每位科學家對那個奇怪訊號都有不同的解讀，所以他們同意在做決定前收集更多數據。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B67","t":"解讀"},{"w":"justification","pos":"n.","def":"a good reason for doing something","cn":"正當理由","s":"The government's ________ for the expensive mission was that it would inspire young people to study science.","zh":"政府對這項昂貴任務的理由是它會激勵年輕人學習科學。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B68","t":"理由"},{"w":"mathematical","pos":"adj.","def":"related to numbers and calculations","cn":"數學的","s":"The scientist used a ________ model to predict the asteroid's path, and the result showed it would safely miss the Earth.","zh":"科學家使用一個數學模型來預測小行星的路徑，而結果顯示它會安全地與地球擦身而過。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B69","t":"數學"},{"w":"modification","pos":"n.","def":"a small change to improve something","cn":"修改；改良","s":"After one ________ to its software, the rover could drive twice as far each day, so the scientists were delighted.","zh":"軟體經過一次修改後，探測車每天能行駛兩倍遠，所以科學家們非常高興。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B70","t":"修改"},{"w":"numerical","pos":"adj.","def":"expressed in numbers","cn":"數字的","s":"The report gave ________ data about each earthquake, but the teacher asked us to explain what the numbers meant.","zh":"報告提供了每場地震的數字資料，但老師要我們解釋這些數字代表什麼意思。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B71","t":"數字"},{"w":"periodic","pos":"adj.","def":"happening again and again at regular times","cn":"週期性的","s":"The volcano shows ________ activity every few years, so the local people are used to small puffs of smoke.","zh":"那座火山每隔幾年就會出現週期性的活動，所以當地人已經習慣小小的冒煙。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B72","t":"週期性的"},{"w":"persistence","pos":"n.","def":"continuing to try even when things are difficult","cn":"堅持","s":"Her ________ finally paid off, because after ten years of searching, she discovered a new comet.","zh":"她的堅持終於有了回報，因為經過十年的搜尋，她發現了一顆新彗星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B73","t":"堅持"},{"w":"precision","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being very exact","cn":"精確","s":"Landing on Mars requires great ________, because even a small mistake could send the rover into a crater.","zh":"登陸火星需要極高的精確度，因為即使是一個小錯誤也可能讓探測車掉進坑洞裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B74","t":"精確度"},{"w":"predictable","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be known in advance","cn":"可預測的","s":"Eclipses are completely ________, but earthquakes are not, so scientists can only give general warnings about them.","zh":"日月蝕是完全可預測的，但地震不是，所以科學家只能對地震發出大致的警告。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B75","t":"可預測的"},{"w":"principally","pos":"adv.","def":"mainly","cn":"主要地","s":"The mission was ________ designed to study the moon's ice, but it also took amazing photos of the Earth.","zh":"這項任務主要是為了研究月球上的冰而設計的，但它也拍下了地球的驚人照片。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B76","t":"主要"},{"w":"proportional","pos":"adj.","def":"changing in size in the same way as something else","cn":"成比例的","s":"The damage from an earthquake is not always ________ to its strength, because building quality matters a lot.","zh":"地震造成的損害不一定與它的強度成比例，因為建築品質非常重要。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B77","t":"成比例"},{"w":"radically","pos":"adv.","def":"in a very big and important way","cn":"徹底地；根本地","s":"Space telescopes have ________ changed our view of the universe, and they keep showing us things nobody expected.","zh":"太空望遠鏡徹底改變了我們對宇宙的看法，而且它們不斷讓我們看到沒人預料到的事物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B78","t":"徹底"},{"w":"reconstruction","pos":"n.","def":"building something again after damage","cn":"重建","s":"The ________ of the town took five years after the earthquake, but the new buildings are much safer.","zh":"地震後小鎮的重建花了五年，但新的建築安全得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B79","t":"重建"},{"w":"relevance","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being connected to what is happening","cn":"關聯性","s":"Some students doubt the ________ of geology, but it helps us understand floods, landslides and earthquakes.","zh":"有些學生懷疑地質學的關聯性，但它幫助我們了解洪水、山崩和地震。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B80","t":"關聯性"},{"w":"reliability","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being trustworthy or working well","cn":"可靠性","s":"The ________ of the old warning system was poor, so the city spent millions on a new one.","zh":"舊預警系統的可靠性很差，所以市政府花了數百萬元建置新的系統。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B81","t":"可靠性"},{"w":"reluctance","pos":"n.","def":"not wanting to do something","cn":"不情願","s":"Despite her ________ to leave home, the family moved away from the volcano, because the experts said it was too dangerous.","zh":"儘管她不願意離開家，那一家人還是搬離了火山，因為專家說那裡太危險了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B82","t":"不願意"},{"w":"representative","pos":"adj.","def":"typical of a larger group","cn":"有代表性的","s":"This rock is ________ of the whole area, so studying it tells us a lot about the history of the region.","zh":"這塊岩石對整個地區具有代表性，所以研究它能讓我們了解許多這個區域的歷史。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B83","t":"代表性"},{"w":"requirement","pos":"n.","def":"something that is needed or necessary","cn":"必要條件；要求","s":"Good eyesight is a ________ for astronauts, but people who wear glasses can still apply in many countries.","zh":"良好的視力是太空人的必要條件，但在許多國家戴眼鏡的人仍然可以申請。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B84","t":"必要條件"},{"w":"resolution","pos":"n.","def":"the amount of detail an image can show","cn":"解析度","s":"The new camera has a much higher ________, so we can now see tiny craters on the moon that were invisible before.","zh":"新相機的解析度高得多，所以我們現在可以看到月球上以前看不見的小坑洞。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B85","t":"解析度"},{"w":"revelation","pos":"n.","def":"a surprising fact that is made known","cn":"揭露；驚人的發現","s":"The photos of Pluto were a ________, because nobody expected to see mountains of ice on such a small world.","zh":"冥王星的照片是一項驚人的發現，因為沒有人預料到會在那麼小的星球上看到冰山。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B86","t":"驚人的發現"},{"w":"significance","pos":"n.","def":"the importance of something","cn":"重要性","s":"The ________ of the discovery was not clear at first, but it later changed the way scientists think about Mars.","zh":"這項發現的重要性起初並不明顯，但後來它改變了科學家對火星的看法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B87","t":"重要性"},{"w":"similarity","pos":"n.","def":"the way in which things are alike","cn":"相似之處","s":"There is a strong ________ between the rocks in Scotland and Canada, so scientists believe the two areas were once joined.","zh":"蘇格蘭和加拿大的岩石之間有很強的相似性，所以科學家相信這兩個地區曾經相連。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B88","t":"相似性"},{"w":"speculation","pos":"n.","def":"guesses made without enough information","cn":"推測；臆測","s":"There was a lot of ________ about the strange object, but it turned out to be an ordinary rock from space.","zh":"關於那個奇怪物體有許多臆測，但結果它只是一塊普通的太空岩石。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B89","t":"臆測"},{"w":"stability","pos":"n.","def":"the state of being steady and not likely to change","cn":"穩定性","s":"Engineers tested the ________ of the bridge carefully, because it must stay standing during strong earthquakes.","zh":"工程師仔細測試了那座橋的穩定性，因為它必須在強烈地震時保持屹立。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B90","t":"穩定性"},{"w":"statistical","pos":"adj.","def":"related to numbers collected to show facts","cn":"統計的","s":"The ________ analysis showed that big earthquakes are rare, but scientists warned that they can still happen at any time.","zh":"統計分析顯示大地震很罕見，但科學家警告它們仍然可能隨時發生。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B91","t":"統計"},{"w":"supplementary","pos":"adj.","def":"added to something to make it complete","cn":"補充的","s":"The teacher gave us ________ reading about black holes, because many students wanted to learn more after the lesson.","zh":"老師給我們關於黑洞的補充閱讀資料，因為許多學生在上完課後想學更多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B92","t":"補充"},{"w":"survival","pos":"n.","def":"the state of continuing to live","cn":"生存","s":"Water and oxygen are essential for ________ in space, so astronauts carefully recycle every drop of water.","zh":"水和氧氣對在太空中生存至關重要，所以太空人仔細回收每一滴水。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B93","t":"生存"},{"w":"temporal","pos":"adj.","def":"related to time","cn":"時間的","s":"The ________ pattern of the earthquakes was strange, because they all happened late at night within one week.","zh":"那些地震的時間模式很奇怪，因為它們都在一週內的深夜發生。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B94","t":"時間"},{"w":"validation","pos":"n.","def":"proof that something is correct or true","cn":"驗證","s":"The theory still needs ________ from other teams, so the scientists shared all their data online.","zh":"這個理論仍需要其他團隊的驗證，所以科學家把所有數據都公開在網路上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B95","t":"驗證"},{"w":"variation","pos":"n.","def":"a change or difference in amount or level","cn":"變化；差異","s":"There is a large ________ in temperature on the moon, because the days are very hot and the nights are freezing.","zh":"月球上的溫度變化很大，因為白天非常熱而夜晚極度寒冷。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B96","t":"變化"},{"w":"verification","pos":"n.","def":"the process of checking that something is true","cn":"核實；查證","s":"The news about the comet needed ________, so the reporter called two astronomers before she wrote her story.","zh":"關於那顆彗星的新聞需要查證，所以記者在寫報導前打電話給兩位天文學家。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B97","t":"查證"},{"w":"visualise","pos":"v.","def":"to form a picture of something in your mind","cn":"想像；視覺化","s":"It is hard to ________ how big the universe is, so our teacher used a football field to show the distances.","zh":"很難想像宇宙有多大，所以我們老師用一座足球場來呈現那些距離。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B98","t":"想像"},{"w":"aberration","pos":"n.","def":"something unusual that is different from what is normal","cn":"異常；偏差","s":"The strange reading was just an ________ caused by a broken sensor, so the scientists did not need to worry.","zh":"那個奇怪的讀數只是一個由故障感測器造成的異常，所以科學家不需要擔心。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B99","t":"異常"},{"w":"adherence","pos":"n.","def":"the act of following rules closely","cn":"遵守","s":"Strict ________ to safety rules saved many lives during the earthquake, and the school became a model for others.","zh":"嚴格遵守安全規定在地震中拯救了許多生命，而這所學校成為其他學校的典範。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B100","t":"遵守"},{"w":"amplitude","pos":"n.","def":"the size of a wave from its middle to its top","cn":"振幅","s":"The ________ of the waves on the seismograph grew very large, so scientists knew the earthquake was strong.","zh":"地震儀上波形的振幅變得非常大，所以科學家知道這場地震很強烈。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B101","t":"振幅"},{"w":"anticipation","pos":"n.","def":"excitement about something that will happen","cn":"期待","s":"There was great ________ before the launch, and thousands of people gathered on the beach to watch.","zh":"發射前充滿了極大的期待，而數千人聚集在海灘上觀看。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B102","t":"期待"},{"w":"conceivably","pos":"adv.","def":"possibly; it can be imagined","cn":"可以想像地；有可能","s":"Life could ________ exist under the ice of Jupiter's moon, so scientists are planning a mission to search for it.","zh":"生命有可能存在於木星衛星的冰層之下，所以科學家正在計畫一項任務去尋找它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B103","t":"有可能"},{"w":"conclusively","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that ends all doubt","cn":"確鑿地；決定性地","s":"The photos ________ proved that the Earth is round, but a few people online still refuse to believe it.","zh":"那些照片確鑿地證明了地球是圓的，但網路上仍有少數人拒絕相信。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B104","t":"確鑿地"},{"w":"conjunction","pos":"n.","def":"when two planets appear very close together in the sky","cn":"（行星）合；結合","s":"Jupiter and Saturn met in a rare ________ in 2020, and many people took photos of the two bright points together.","zh":"木星和土星在2020年發生了一次罕見的合，而許多人拍下了兩個亮點並排的照片。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B105","t":"合"},{"w":"contingency","pos":"n.","def":"a possible future event that you must plan for","cn":"意外情況；應變","s":"The astronauts trained for every ________, so they knew exactly what to do when the alarm suddenly rang.","zh":"太空人針對每一種意外情況受過訓練，所以當警報突然響起時，他們清楚知道該怎麼做。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B106","t":"意外情況"},{"w":"contour","pos":"n.","def":"the outline or shape of something","cn":"輪廓","s":"We could see the ________ of the mountains against the sunset, and the sky behind them turned bright orange.","zh":"我們可以看到夕陽映襯下的山脈輪廓，而它們後面的天空變成了亮橘色。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B107","t":"輪廓"},{"w":"convergence","pos":"n.","def":"the act of moving toward the same point","cn":"匯聚；聚合","s":"The ________ of two plates pushes the land upward, so high mountains often form where plates meet.","zh":"兩個板塊的聚合把陸地往上推，所以高山常常在板塊交會的地方形成。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B108","t":"聚合"},{"w":"culmination","pos":"n.","def":"the final result of a long process","cn":"頂點；成果","s":"The landing on Mars was the ________ of twenty years of hard work, so many engineers cried with happiness.","zh":"登陸火星是二十年辛勤工作的成果，所以許多工程師喜極而泣。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B109","t":"成果"},{"w":"curvature","pos":"n.","def":"the amount that something is curved","cn":"曲率；彎曲度","s":"From a high plane you can see the ________ of the Earth, but from the ground the horizon looks completely flat.","zh":"從高空的飛機上你可以看到地球的弧度，但從地面看地平線卻完全是平的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B110","t":"弧度"},{"w":"discernible","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be seen or noticed, but not easily","cn":"可察覺的","s":"The comet's tail was barely ________ in the city sky, so we drove to the countryside for a better view.","zh":"彗星的尾巴在城市的天空中幾乎看不出來，所以我們開車到鄉下去看得更清楚。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B111","t":"看不出來"},{"w":"dispersal","pos":"n.","def":"the spreading of things over a wide area","cn":"散布；擴散","s":"The wind caused the wide ________ of volcanic ash, and cars in cities far away were covered in grey dust.","zh":"風造成火山灰大範圍擴散，而遠方城市的汽車都覆蓋著灰色的塵土。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B112","t":"擴散"},{"w":"divergence","pos":"n.","def":"the act of moving apart in different directions","cn":"分離；分歧","s":"The ________ of two plates in Iceland creates new land, so the island is slowly getting wider.","zh":"冰島兩個板塊的分離產生新的陸地，所以這座島正慢慢變寬。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B113","t":"分離"},{"w":"elongated","pos":"adj.","def":"longer than usual and thin","cn":"拉長的；細長的","s":"The strange object from space had an ________ shape like a cigar, and scientists still argue about what it was.","zh":"那個來自太空的奇怪物體有著像雪茄一樣細長的形狀，而科學家至今仍在爭論它是什麼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B114","t":"細長的"},{"w":"frontier","pos":"n.","def":"the edge of what is known or explored","cn":"前沿；邊疆","s":"Space is often called the final ________, because it is the last great place that humans have not explored.","zh":"太空常被稱為最後的邊疆，因為那是人類最後一個尚未探索的偉大地方。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B115","t":"邊疆"},{"w":"inconceivable","pos":"adj.","def":"impossible to imagine or believe","cn":"難以想像的","s":"A hundred years ago, sending people to the moon was ________, but today companies sell tickets to space.","zh":"一百年前，把人送上月球是難以想像的，但今天公司在販售太空之旅的票。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B116","t":"難以想像的"},{"w":"indefinite","pos":"adj.","def":"without a fixed end or limit","cn":"無限期的","s":"The trail is closed for an ________ period after the landslide, so hikers must choose another route for now.","zh":"山崩後那條步道無限期封閉，所以健行者目前必須選擇另一條路線。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B117","t":"無限期"},{"w":"inexplicable","pos":"adj.","def":"impossible to explain","cn":"無法解釋的","s":"The flashing light in the sky seemed ________, but it was later identified as a satellite reflecting sunlight.","zh":"天空中閃爍的光看似無法解釋，但後來被確認是一顆反射陽光的人造衛星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B118","t":"無法解釋"},{"w":"infinitesimal","pos":"adj.","def":"extremely small","cn":"極微小的","s":"The chance of a large asteroid hitting Earth this year is ________, so there is no need to panic.","zh":"今年大型小行星撞擊地球的機率極小，所以沒有必要驚慌。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B119","t":"極小"},{"w":"insignificant","pos":"adj.","def":"too small or unimportant to matter","cn":"微不足道的","s":"Looking at photos of the universe makes our daily problems seem ________, and that can actually be comforting.","zh":"看著宇宙的照片會讓我們日常的煩惱顯得微不足道，而這其實能讓人感到安慰。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B120","t":"微不足道"},{"w":"intangible","pos":"adj.","def":"not physical, but still real","cn":"無形的","s":"The benefits of space research are sometimes ________, because they include inspiration and curiosity, not just new products.","zh":"太空研究的好處有時是無形的，因為它們包括啟發和好奇心，而不只是新產品。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B121","t":"無形的"},{"w":"invert","pos":"v.","def":"to turn something upside down","cn":"倒轉；顛倒","s":"Telescopes often ________ the image of the moon, so beginners are confused when everything looks upside down.","zh":"望遠鏡常常把月亮的影像顛倒過來，所以初學者看到一切都是倒的時會很困惑。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B122","t":"顛倒"},{"w":"irregularity","pos":"n.","def":"something that is not normal or regular","cn":"不規則；異常","s":"The engineer noticed an ________ in the engine data, so the launch was delayed until the problem was fixed.","zh":"工程師注意到引擎數據中有一個異常，所以發射被延後直到問題解決。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B123","t":"異常"},{"w":"marvel","pos":"v.","def":"to feel great surprise and admiration","cn":"驚嘆","s":"Visitors ________ at the huge crystals in the cave, and many of them say it is the most beautiful place they have seen.","zh":"遊客對洞穴裡巨大的晶體驚嘆不已，而許多人說那是他們見過最美的地方。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B124","t":"驚嘆"},{"w":"oblique","pos":"adj.","def":"at an angle; not straight","cn":"傾斜的；斜的","s":"The photo was taken from an ________ angle, so the crater looks much deeper than it really is.","zh":"這張照片是從斜角度拍攝的，所以火山口看起來比實際深得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B125","t":"斜"},{"w":"oscillate","pos":"v.","def":"to move backwards and forwards regularly","cn":"擺動；振盪","s":"Tall buildings ________ slowly during strong earthquakes, but this movement actually helps them avoid serious damage.","zh":"高樓在強烈地震中會緩慢地擺動，但這種晃動其實能幫助它們避免嚴重損壞。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B126","t":"擺動"},{"w":"perpendicular","pos":"adj.","def":"at an angle of 90 degrees to something","cn":"垂直的","s":"The walls of the canyon are almost ________ to the river, so climbing them requires special equipment.","zh":"峽谷的岩壁幾乎與河流垂直，所以攀爬它們需要特殊裝備。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B127","t":"垂直"},{"w":"radiate","pos":"v.","def":"to send out heat or light in all directions","cn":"散發；輻射","s":"The sun ________ energy in every direction, but only a tiny part of it reaches the Earth.","zh":"太陽向四面八方散發能量，但只有很小一部分到達地球。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B128","t":"散發"},{"w":"resemblance","pos":"n.","def":"the state of looking similar to something","cn":"相似","s":"The desert in Chile has a strong ________ to the surface of Mars, so space agencies test their rovers there.","zh":"智利的沙漠與火星表面非常相似，所以太空機構在那裡測試他們的探測車。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B129","t":"相似"},{"w":"revolutionary","pos":"adj.","def":"completely new and causing great change","cn":"革命性的","s":"The telescope was a ________ invention, because it allowed Galileo to see the moons of Jupiter for the first time.","zh":"望遠鏡是一項革命性的發明，因為它讓伽利略第一次看到木星的衛星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B130","t":"革命性的"},{"w":"simultaneously","pos":"adv.","def":"at the same time","cn":"同時地","s":"The two telescopes recorded the explosion ________, so scientists could compare the results from different places.","zh":"兩架望遠鏡同時記錄了那次爆炸，所以科學家可以比較來自不同地方的結果。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B131","t":"同時"},{"w":"void","pos":"n.","def":"a large empty space","cn":"空無；真空","s":"Space is not a complete ________, because it contains thin gas, dust and radiation everywhere.","zh":"太空並不是完全的真空，因為到處都有稀薄的氣體、塵埃和輻射。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B132","t":"真空"},{"w":"acceleration","pos":"n.","def":"the process of going faster","cn":"加速","s":"The ________ during launch pushed the astronauts back into their seats, and they felt three times heavier than usual.","zh":"發射時的加速把太空人壓回座位上，而他們覺得自己比平常重了三倍。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B133","t":"加速"},{"w":"alignment","pos":"n.","def":"the arrangement of things in a straight line","cn":"排成一直線；對齊","s":"The rare ________ of five planets made headlines, and people around the world went outside before dawn to see it.","zh":"五顆行星罕見地排成一直線登上了新聞頭條，而世界各地的人在黎明前走到戶外觀看。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B134","t":"排成一直線"},{"w":"attraction","pos":"n.","def":"a force that pulls things toward each other","cn":"吸引力","s":"The ________ between the Earth and the moon causes ocean tides, so fishermen pay close attention to the moon's phases.","zh":"地球和月球之間的吸引力造成海洋潮汐，所以漁民非常注意月亮的盈虧。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B135","t":"吸引力"},{"w":"calculation","pos":"n.","def":"the process of using numbers to find an answer","cn":"計算","s":"One wrong ________ caused the spacecraft to crash, because the engineers had mixed up two different units.","zh":"一個錯誤的計算導致太空船墜毀，因為工程師搞混了兩種不同的單位。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B136","t":"計算"},{"w":"circular","pos":"adj.","def":"shaped like a circle","cn":"圓形的","s":"Most craters on the moon are ________, but a few are long because the space rock hit the surface at a low angle.","zh":"月球上大多數坑洞是圓形的，但少數是長條形的，因為太空岩石以低角度撞擊表面。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B137","t":"圓形的"},{"w":"classify","pos":"v.","def":"to put things into groups by type","cn":"分類","s":"Geologists ________ rocks into three main groups, and each group forms in a completely different way.","zh":"地質學家把岩石分類成三大類，而每一類的形成方式都完全不同。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B138","t":"分類"},{"w":"collide","pos":"v.","def":"to hit something with force","cn":"相撞","s":"When two plates ________, the land is pushed upward, and this is how many great mountain ranges were formed.","zh":"當兩個板塊相撞時，陸地會被往上推，而許多大山脈就是這樣形成的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B139","t":"相撞"},{"w":"compression","pos":"n.","def":"the act of pressing something into a smaller space","cn":"壓縮","s":"Deep underground, the ________ of rock layers creates great heat, and over time this changes one rock type into another.","zh":"在地底深處，岩層的壓縮產生巨大的熱，而隨著時間這會把一種岩石轉變成另一種。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B140","t":"壓縮"},{"w":"continuous","pos":"adj.","def":"happening without stopping","cn":"持續不斷的","s":"The volcano has been in ________ eruption for months, so the lava has slowly built a new piece of land.","zh":"那座火山已經持續不斷地噴發好幾個月，所以熔岩慢慢地堆積出一塊新陸地。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B141","t":"持續不斷地"},{"w":"contradictory","pos":"adj.","def":"disagreeing with each other","cn":"互相矛盾的","s":"The two news reports gave ________ information about the earthquake, so I checked the official website instead.","zh":"兩則新聞報導對那場地震提供了互相矛盾的資訊，所以我改查官方網站。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B142","t":"互相矛盾的"},{"w":"debatable","pos":"adj.","def":"not certain and open to discussion","cn":"有爭議的","s":"Whether Pluto should be a planet is still ________, and some scientists want to change the definition again.","zh":"冥王星是否應該算是行星仍然有爭議，而且有些科學家想再次修改定義。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B143","t":"有爭議"},{"w":"deliberately","pos":"adv.","def":"on purpose","cn":"故意地；刻意地","s":"The engineers ________ crashed the old spacecraft into the sea, because they did not want it to become space junk.","zh":"工程師故意讓那艘舊太空船墜入海中，因為他們不希望它變成太空垃圾。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B144","t":"故意"},{"w":"dense","pos":"adj.","def":"heavy for its size; tightly packed","cn":"稠密的；密度高的","s":"The Earth's core is very ________, so it sank to the centre of the planet when the Earth was young.","zh":"地核的密度非常高，所以在地球還年輕時它就沉到了地球中心。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B145","t":"密度"},{"w":"dissolve","pos":"v.","def":"to mix completely into a liquid","cn":"溶解","s":"Rainwater slowly ________ limestone over thousands of years, and this process creates beautiful caves underground.","zh":"雨水在數千年間慢慢溶解石灰岩，而這個過程在地下形成美麗的洞穴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B146","t":"溶解"},{"w":"distant","pos":"adj.","def":"far away","cn":"遙遠的","s":"Light from ________ galaxies takes billions of years to reach us, so we see them as they were long ago.","zh":"來自遙遠星系的光需要數十億年才能到達我們這裡，所以我們看到的是它們很久以前的樣子。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B147","t":"遙遠"},{"w":"disturbance","pos":"n.","def":"something that interrupts normal conditions","cn":"干擾；擾動","s":"The solar storm caused a ________ to phone signals, so some people could not make calls for a few hours.","zh":"太陽風暴對手機訊號造成了干擾，所以有些人好幾個小時無法打電話。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B148","t":"干擾"},{"w":"eject","pos":"v.","def":"to push or throw something out with force","cn":"噴出；彈出","s":"Volcanoes can ________ rocks as big as cars, so the area near the crater is extremely dangerous during an eruption.","zh":"火山可以噴出像汽車那麼大的岩石，所以噴發期間火山口附近的區域極度危險。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B149","t":"噴出"},{"w":"enclose","pos":"v.","def":"to surround something completely","cn":"圍住；封閉","s":"Thick walls ________ the telescope, but the roof can open at night so it can point at the sky.","zh":"厚厚的牆壁圍住那架望遠鏡，但屋頂在晚上可以打開，讓它能夠對準天空。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B150","t":"圍住"},{"w":"faint","pos":"adj.","def":"not strong or clear; hard to see or hear","cn":"微弱的；模糊的","s":"The star was so ________ that we could not see it with our eyes, but the telescope showed it clearly.","zh":"那顆星星非常微弱，所以我們用肉眼看不到它，但望遠鏡清楚地顯示了它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B151","t":"微弱"},{"w":"fuse","pos":"v.","def":"to join together, often by heat","cn":"融合","s":"Inside the sun, small atoms ________ together, and this process releases the huge energy that gives us light.","zh":"在太陽內部，小原子融合在一起，而這個過程釋放出給我們光亮的巨大能量。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B152","t":"融合"},{"w":"horizontal","pos":"adj.","def":"flat and level, parallel to the ground","cn":"水平的","s":"The rock layers were ________ at first, but strong pressure later bent them into curves.","zh":"這些岩層起初是水平的，但後來強大的壓力把它們擠彎成曲線。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B153","t":"水平的"},{"w":"immensely","pos":"adv.","def":"extremely; very much","cn":"極其；非常","s":"The documentary about black holes was ________ popular, so the channel decided to make a second series.","zh":"那部關於黑洞的紀錄片極其受歡迎，所以頻道決定製作第二季。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B154","t":"極其"},{"w":"incline","pos":"n.","def":"a slope","cn":"斜坡","s":"The rover slowly climbed a steep ________, but the engineers stopped it when its wheels began to slip.","zh":"探測車慢慢爬上一個陡峭的斜坡，但當它的輪子開始打滑時，工程師讓它停了下來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B155","t":"斜坡"},{"w":"indirectly","pos":"adv.","def":"not in a direct way","cn":"間接地","s":"Scientists study black holes ________, because they cannot see them, so they watch how nearby stars move instead.","zh":"科學家間接地研究黑洞，因為他們看不到黑洞，所以他們改為觀察附近恆星的移動方式。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B156","t":"間接地"},{"w":"insulate","pos":"v.","def":"to cover something to keep heat in or out","cn":"隔熱；絕緣","s":"Engineers ________ the rover with special material, because nights on Mars are cold enough to break its parts.","zh":"工程師用特殊材料為探測車隔熱，因為火星的夜晚冷到足以弄壞它的零件。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B157","t":"隔熱"},{"w":"theorise","pos":"v.","def":"to form an idea to explain something","cn":"建立理論；推論","s":"Some scientists ________ that the moon was formed after a planet crashed into the young Earth, and many agree with them.","zh":"有些科學家推論月球是在一顆行星撞上年輕的地球之後形成的，而許多人同意他們的看法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B158","t":"推論"},{"w":"microscopic","pos":"adj.","def":"so small that it can only be seen with a microscope","cn":"微小的；顯微鏡才能看見的","s":"The space dust is ________, but it hits spacecraft at such high speed that it can still cause damage.","zh":"太空塵埃極其微小，但它以極高的速度撞擊太空船，所以仍能造成損害。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B159","t":"極其微小"},{"w":"molecular","pos":"adj.","def":"related to molecules","cn":"分子的","s":"The team studied the ________ structure of the meteorite, and they found chemicals that are important for life.","zh":"團隊研究了那顆隕石的分子結構，而他們發現了對生命很重要的化學物質。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B160","t":"分子"},{"w":"occasional","pos":"adj.","def":"happening sometimes but not often","cn":"偶爾的","s":"Taiwan has ________ strong earthquakes, so families are advised to keep water and torches at home.","zh":"臺灣偶爾會有強烈地震，所以家家戶戶被建議在家裡準備水和手電筒。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B161","t":"偶爾"},{"w":"particle","pos":"n.","def":"a very small piece of something","cn":"粒子；微粒","s":"Each ________ of volcanic ash is tiny and sharp, so it can hurt your lungs if you breathe it in.","zh":"每一顆火山灰微粒都很小又尖銳，所以如果吸進去會傷害你的肺。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B162","t":"微粒"},{"w":"penetrate","pos":"v.","def":"to go into or through something","cn":"穿透","s":"Radio waves can ________ thick clouds of dust, so radio telescopes can see parts of the galaxy that are hidden from normal ones.","zh":"無線電波可以穿透厚厚的塵埃雲，所以電波望遠鏡能看到一般望遠鏡看不到的銀河部分。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B163","t":"穿透"},{"w":"plunge","pos":"v.","def":"to fall or drop suddenly","cn":"驟降；跳入","s":"Temperatures on the moon ________ to minus 170 degrees at night, so future bases will need excellent heating.","zh":"月球上的溫度在夜晚會驟降到零下一百七十度，所以未來的基地需要非常好的暖氣系統。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B164","t":"驟降"},{"w":"undetected","pos":"adj.","def":"not noticed or discovered","cn":"未被察覺的","s":"The small asteroid passed the Earth ________, and scientists only discovered it two days later.","zh":"那顆小行星在未被察覺的情況下經過地球，而科學家兩天後才發現它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B165","t":"未被察覺"},{"w":"primarily","pos":"adv.","def":"mainly","cn":"主要地","s":"The island's economy depends ________ on tourism, so the volcano is both a danger and a valuable attraction.","zh":"這座島的經濟主要仰賴觀光，所以那座火山既是危險，也是珍貴的觀光景點。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B166","t":"主要"},{"w":"resistant","pos":"adj.","def":"not easily damaged or affected by something","cn":"抗……的；耐……的","s":"The new school is ________ to earthquakes, and parents feel much safer now that their children study there.","zh":"新的學校能抵抗地震，而家長們現在對孩子在那裡讀書感到安心得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B167","t":"能抵抗"},{"w":"solid","pos":"adj.","def":"hard and firm, not liquid or gas","cn":"固態的","s":"The moon has a ________ surface, but Jupiter does not, so no spacecraft can ever land on Jupiter.","zh":"月球有固態表面，但木星沒有，所以沒有任何太空船能在木星上降落。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B168","t":"固態"},{"w":"stationary","pos":"adj.","def":"not moving","cn":"靜止的","s":"Some satellites seem ________ in the sky, but they are actually moving at the same speed as the Earth spins.","zh":"有些人造衛星在天空中看似靜止，但它們其實是以和地球自轉相同的速度移動。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B169","t":"靜止"},{"w":"theoretically","pos":"adv.","def":"according to theory, but not yet proven in practice","cn":"理論上","s":"Time travel is ________ possible according to some scientists, but nobody knows how to actually do it.","zh":"根據某些科學家的說法，時間旅行理論上是可能的，但沒有人知道實際上該怎麼做。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B170","t":"理論上"},{"w":"tremendous","pos":"adj.","def":"very great in size or amount","cn":"巨大的；極大的","s":"The eruption released a ________ amount of energy, and the sound was heard over a thousand kilometres away.","zh":"那次噴發釋放了巨大的能量，而聲音在一千多公里外都聽得到。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B171","t":"巨大的"},{"w":"uneven","pos":"adj.","def":"not flat or smooth","cn":"不平坦的","s":"The ground on Mars is rocky and ________, so the rover moves very slowly to avoid getting stuck.","zh":"火星上的地面多岩石又不平坦，所以探測車移動得非常緩慢以免卡住。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B172","t":"不平坦"},{"w":"unstable","pos":"adj.","def":"likely to change, move or fall","cn":"不穩定的","s":"The cliff became ________ after the earthquake, so the beach below was closed for the rest of the summer.","zh":"那座懸崖在地震後變得不穩定，所以下方的海灘在夏天剩下的時間都封閉了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B173","t":"不穩定"},{"w":"vertical","pos":"adj.","def":"going straight up and down","cn":"垂直的","s":"The climbers faced a ________ wall of rock, but they reached the top safely because they had trained for months.","zh":"攀岩者面對一面垂直的岩壁，但他們安全抵達頂端，因為他們已經訓練了好幾個月。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B174","t":"垂直的"},{"w":"vibrate","pos":"v.","def":"to shake with small fast movements","cn":"震動","s":"The windows started to ________ during the earthquake, and our dog ran under the table before we did.","zh":"地震時窗戶開始震動，而我們的狗比我們先跑到桌子底下。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B175","t":"震動"},{"w":"visibility","pos":"n.","def":"how far or how well you can see","cn":"能見度","s":"________ was very poor because of the volcanic ash, so drivers turned on their lights in the middle of the day.","zh":"因為火山灰，能見度非常差，所以駕駛人在大白天打開了車燈。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B176","t":"能見度"},{"w":"apparently","pos":"adv.","def":"according to what you have heard or read","cn":"據說；看來","s":"The Northern Lights were ________ visible as far south as Japan last night, but I missed them because I was asleep.","zh":"據說昨晚在南至日本的地方都看得到北極光，但我錯過了，因為我在睡覺。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B177","t":"據說"},{"w":"assertion","pos":"n.","def":"a strong statement that something is true","cn":"主張；斷言","s":"His ________ that the moon landing was fake was quickly proven wrong, because the evidence for it is overwhelming.","zh":"他認為登月是造假的主張很快就被證明是錯的，因為支持登月的證據壓倒性地多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B178","t":"主張"},{"w":"comparatively","pos":"adv.","def":"when compared with something else","cn":"相對地；比較而言","s":"Mars is ________ close to Earth, so it is the most likely planet for humans to visit first.","zh":"火星離地球相對較近，所以它是人類最有可能首先造訪的行星。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B179","t":"相對"},{"w":"conceptual","pos":"adj.","def":"related to ideas rather than real objects","cn":"概念上的","s":"The engineers showed a ________ design for a moon base, but they admitted that building it would take decades.","zh":"工程師展示了一個月球基地的概念設計，但他們承認建造它需要數十年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B180","t":"概念"},{"w":"consistency","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of always behaving or performing in the same way","cn":"一致性","s":"The ________ of the results gave the team confidence, because every test produced almost the same numbers.","zh":"結果的一致性讓團隊有信心，因為每次測試都得出幾乎相同的數字。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B181","t":"一致性"},{"w":"contested","pos":"adj.","def":"argued about; not agreed on by everyone","cn":"有爭議的","s":"The age of the rocks is still ________, so two research teams are testing new samples to settle the question.","zh":"那些岩石的年代仍然有爭議，所以兩個研究團隊正在檢測新的樣本以解決這個問題。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B182","t":"有爭議"},{"w":"durability","pos":"n.","def":"the ability to last a long time without breaking","cn":"耐用性","s":"The ________ of the rover's wheels surprised everyone, because they lasted for years on the sharp Martian rocks.","zh":"探測車輪子的耐用性讓所有人驚訝，因為它們在尖銳的火星岩石上撐了好幾年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B183","t":"耐用性"},{"w":"evolutionary","pos":"adj.","def":"related to the slow development of living things","cn":"演化的","s":"Fossils show the ________ history of life on Earth, and they help us understand how animals changed over time.","zh":"化石顯示地球上生命的演化歷史，而它們幫助我們了解動物如何隨時間改變。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B184","t":"演化"},{"w":"exceedingly","pos":"adv.","def":"extremely; very","cn":"極其；非常","s":"The journey to Mars is ________ long, so astronauts will need to be mentally strong as well as physically fit.","zh":"前往火星的旅程極其漫長，所以太空人不但身體要健康，心理也必須很堅強。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B185","t":"極其"},{"w":"explanatory","pos":"adj.","def":"giving an explanation","cn":"解釋性的","s":"The museum added ________ videos next to each rock, so visitors can understand how it was formed.","zh":"博物館在每塊岩石旁加上了解說影片，讓參觀者能了解它是如何形成的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B186","t":"解說"},{"w":"exploratory","pos":"adj.","def":"done to find out more about something","cn":"探索性的；勘查的","s":"The company sent an ________ team to the island, and they found signs of a hot spring under the ground.","zh":"那家公司派了一支勘查團隊到島上，而他們發現地下有溫泉的跡象。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B187","t":"勘查"},{"w":"finding","pos":"n.","def":"a piece of information discovered after research","cn":"研究發現","s":"The latest ________ suggests that Mars once had a large ocean, so scientists want to look for ancient life there.","zh":"最新的研究發現指出火星曾經有一片大海洋，所以科學家想在那裡尋找古代生命。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B188","t":"研究發現"},{"w":"fundamentally","pos":"adv.","def":"in a very basic and important way","cn":"根本上","s":"The discovery ________ changed our view of the Earth, because it showed that continents are not fixed in place.","zh":"這項發現根本上改變了我們對地球的看法，因為它顯示大陸並不是固定不動的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B189","t":"根本上"},{"w":"generalisation","pos":"n.","def":"a statement that is true in most cases but not all","cn":"概括；以偏概全的說法","s":"It is a ________ to say that all deserts are hot, because Antarctica is also a desert and it is freezing.","zh":"說所有沙漠都很熱是一種以偏概全的說法，因為南極洲也是沙漠，而且它冰冷無比。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B190","t":"以偏概全的說法"},{"w":"improbable","pos":"adj.","def":"not likely to happen","cn":"不太可能的","s":"A direct hit from a large asteroid is ________, but space agencies still practise ways to push one off course.","zh":"被大型小行星直接撞擊是不太可能的，但太空機構仍然演練將小行星推離軌道的方法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B191","t":"不太可能的"},{"w":"inaccurate","pos":"adj.","def":"not correct or exact","cn":"不準確的","s":"The old map was ________, so we got lost on the mountain, and we only found the trail again after an hour.","zh":"那張舊地圖不準確，所以我們在山上迷路了，而我們一小時後才再找到步道。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B192","t":"不準確"},{"w":"indisputable","pos":"adj.","def":"so clearly true that nobody can argue about it","cn":"無可爭辯的","s":"The evidence that the Earth goes around the sun is ________, but people believed the opposite for thousands of years.","zh":"地球繞著太陽轉的證據是無可爭辯的，但人們在數千年間都相信相反的說法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B193","t":"無可爭辯的"},{"w":"inevitably","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that cannot be avoided","cn":"不可避免地","s":"Old satellites ________ fall back toward the Earth, but most of them burn up completely in the atmosphere.","zh":"舊的人造衛星不可避免地會落回地球，但它們大多數會在大氣層中完全燒毀。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B194","t":"不可避免地"},{"w":"intriguing","pos":"adj.","def":"very interesting because it is unusual","cn":"引人入勝的；耐人尋味的","s":"The rover found an ________ rock with strange patterns, so the scientists decided to study it more closely.","zh":"探測車發現了一塊帶有奇特圖案、耐人尋味的岩石，所以科學家決定更仔細地研究它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B195","t":"耐人尋味的"},{"w":"limitless","pos":"adj.","def":"without any limit","cn":"無限的","s":"The young astronomer had ________ energy, and she often stayed at the observatory until sunrise.","zh":"那位年輕的天文學家有著無窮的精力，而她常常在天文臺待到日出。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B196","t":"無窮的"},{"w":"mysterious","pos":"adj.","def":"strange and difficult to understand","cn":"神秘的","s":"Dark matter is one of the most ________ things in science, because we know it exists but cannot see it.","zh":"暗物質是科學中最神秘的東西之一，因為我們知道它存在，但卻看不到它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B197","t":"神秘"},{"w":"observable","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be seen or noticed","cn":"可觀測的","s":"The ________ universe is huge, but scientists believe much more exists beyond what we can see.","zh":"可觀測的宇宙非常巨大，但科學家相信在我們能看到的範圍之外還存在更多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B198","t":"可觀測的"},{"w":"reportedly","pos":"adv.","def":"according to what people say","cn":"據報導","s":"The company is ________ planning a hotel in space, but it has not shared any details or prices yet.","zh":"據報導那家公司正計畫在太空中建造一間旅館，但它還沒有公布任何細節或價格。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B199","t":"據報導"},{"w":"plausibly","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that seems reasonable or likely","cn":"合理地；似乎可信地","s":"The scientist ________ explained why the lake had disappeared, and her theory was later supported by satellite photos.","zh":"那位科學家合理地解釋了湖泊消失的原因，而她的理論後來得到衛星照片的支持。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B200","t":"合理地"},{"w":"down to earth","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"practical, sensible and friendly","cn":"務實的；平易近人的","s":"The famous astronaut was very ______ ______ ______, and she happily answered every question the students asked her.","zh":"那位知名太空人非常平易近人，而且她很樂意回答學生問她的每一個問題。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P1","t":"平易近人"},{"w":"over the moon","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"extremely happy","cn":"欣喜若狂","s":"My brother was ______ ______ ______ when he was accepted to study astronomy, so he called everyone in the family that night.","zh":"我哥哥被錄取念天文學時欣喜若狂，所以他當晚打電話給家裡每一個人。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P2","t":"欣喜若狂"},{"w":"once in a blue moon","pos":"phr.","def":"very rarely","cn":"千載難逢；極少","s":"We see the Northern Lights in Taiwan only ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, so most people travel abroad to watch them.","zh":"我們在臺灣極少能看到北極光，所以大多數人會出國去觀賞。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P3","t":"極少"},{"w":"reach for the stars","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to try to achieve something very difficult","cn":"追求遠大目標","s":"Our teacher always tells us to ______ ______ ______ ______, because she believes that hard work can make big dreams come true.","zh":"我們老師總是告訴我們要追求遠大的目標，因為她相信努力能讓遠大的夢想成真。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P4","t":"追求遠大的目標"},{"w":"the sky's the limit","pos":"phr.","def":"there is no limit to what can be achieved","cn":"前途無量；沒有極限","s":"You are talented and hardworking, so ______ ______ ______ ______ for your future in science.","zh":"你有天分又努力，所以你在科學領域的未來前途無量。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P5","t":"前途無量"},{"w":"light years ahead of","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"much more advanced than","cn":"遙遙領先","s":"The new space telescope is ______ ______ ______ ______ older models, and it has already found hundreds of new galaxies.","zh":"新的太空望遠鏡比舊型號遙遙領先，而它已經發現了數百個新星系。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P6","t":"遙遙領先"},{"w":"move heaven and earth","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to do everything possible to achieve something","cn":"竭盡全力","s":"The rescue teams ______ ______ ______ ______ to find survivors after the earthquake, and they worked for days without rest.","zh":"地震後救援隊竭盡全力尋找倖存者，而他們好幾天不眠不休地工作。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P7","t":"竭盡全力"},{"w":"on shaky ground","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"not based on strong facts or not certain","cn":"基礎不穩；站不住腳","s":"His argument was ______ ______ ______, because he had no real evidence that animals can predict earthquakes.","zh":"他的論點站不住腳，因為他沒有真正的證據證明動物能預測地震。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P8","t":"站不住腳"},{"w":"it's not rocket science","pos":"phr.","def":"it is not difficult to understand","cn":"這並不難懂","s":"Packing an emergency kit is easy, and ______ ______ ______ ______, so every family should prepare one this weekend.","zh":"準備緊急避難包很容易，而且這並不難，所以每個家庭這個週末都應該準備一個。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P9","t":"這並不難"},{"w":"out of this world","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"extremely good","cn":"好得不得了","s":"The view of the stars from the mountain was ______ ______ ______ ______, and we stayed outside until midnight despite the cold.","zh":"從山上看星星的景色好得不得了，而儘管很冷，我們仍在戶外待到午夜。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P10","t":"好得不得了"},{"w":"thank one's lucky stars","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to feel very grateful for good luck","cn":"慶幸自己走運","s":"We ______ ______ ______ ______ that nobody was hurt in the earthquake, because the old shop next door completely collapsed.","zh":"我們慶幸自己很走運，地震中沒有人受傷，因為隔壁的老店完全倒塌了。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P11","t":"慶幸自己很走運"},{"w":"break new ground","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to do something new that nobody has done before","cn":"開創新局；有所突破","s":"The young scientists ______ ______ ______ with their study of moon dust, and their work was published in a famous journal.","zh":"那些年輕科學家以他們對月球塵土的研究開創了新局，而他們的成果發表在一本知名期刊上。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P12","t":"開創了新局"},{"w":"come back down to earth","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to return to normal life after an exciting time","cn":"回到現實","s":"After the amazing trip to the observatory, it was hard to ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, because we had a math test the next day.","zh":"在天文臺的精彩旅程之後，很難回到現實，因為我們隔天有數學考試。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P13","t":"回到現實"},{"w":"move mountains","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to achieve something that seems impossible","cn":"移山倒海；成就不可能的事","s":"With enough teamwork, a small group of students can ______ ______, and our robot club proved this by winning the national prize.","zh":"只要有足夠的團隊合作，一小群學生也能成就不可能的事，而我們的機器人社團贏得全國大獎證明了這一點。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P14","t":"成就不可能的事"},{"w":"rock solid","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"very strong, reliable and unlikely to fail","cn":"堅如磐石；極其可靠","s":"The scientists' evidence was ______ ______, so even the most doubtful reviewers accepted their surprising conclusion.","zh":"科學家的證據極其可靠，所以即使是最多疑的審查者也接受了他們令人驚訝的結論。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P15","t":"極其可靠"},{"w":"earth-shattering","pos":"adj.","def":"extremely important or shocking","cn":"驚天動地的","s":"The discovery of water on Mars was ________ news, and it appeared on the front page of every newspaper.","zh":"在火星上發現水是驚天動地的新聞，而它登上了每一份報紙的頭版。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P16","t":"驚天動地的"},{"w":"blow one's top","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to suddenly become very angry","cn":"勃然大怒","s":"My dad ______ ______ ______ when he saw the broken telescope, but he calmed down after my brother said sorry.","zh":"我爸爸看到摔壞的望遠鏡時勃然大怒，但在我哥哥道歉後他就冷靜下來了。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P17","t":"勃然大怒"},{"w":"the calm before the storm","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a quiet period before trouble or great activity","cn":"暴風雨前的寧靜","s":"The office was silent an hour before the launch, but everyone knew it was only ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"發射前一小時辦公室一片寂靜，但每個人都知道那只是暴風雨前的寧靜。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P18","t":"暴風雨前的寧靜"},{"w":"shake the foundations of","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to seriously challenge basic ideas or systems","cn":"動搖……的根基","s":"The new theory could ______ ______ ______ ______ modern physics, so many scientists are checking it very carefully.","zh":"這個新理論可能會動搖現代物理學的根基，所以許多科學家正非常仔細地檢驗它。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P19","t":"動搖 根基"},{"w":"the centre of the universe","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the most important person or thing (often used critically)","cn":"宇宙的中心；自以為最重要","s":"He acts as if he is ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, but his teammates are tired of his selfish attitude.","zh":"他表現得好像自己是宇宙的中心，但他的隊友已經厭倦了他自私的態度。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P20","t":"宇宙的中心"}]};
